1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ⚠️ '''Warning: Hypothetical Origin!'''
2 CONT Information regarding the identity, name, and parentage of Thore Reidarssøn's wife is a subject of long-standing debate in Norwegian genealogy and is based purely on circumstantial evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT 📌 '''The Issue of Name and Identity'''
2 CONT * In the original works of researcher Otto Winther, this woman appears simply as the "Unknown daughter of Eivind from Faale" ('''Ukjent Faale Eivindsdatter''').
2 CONT * The name '''Rønnaug''' is not verified by contemporary 14th-century primary sources and represents a later reconstruction.
2 CONT
2 CONT 📜 '''Theory of Parentage and Kinship (and its problems)'''
2 CONT According to the most widespread old hypothesis, she was listed as the daughter of ''Eyvind Tjostolvsson Bolt'' and ''Anna Ranesdatter Fåle''. This would theoretically make her the sister of:
2 CONT * '''Lodin Eivindssøn (Kusse)''' (d. 1375), married to Ingeborg Sigurdsdatter Kane.
2 CONT * '''Rane Eivindssøn''', married to Aasa Salmundsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''However, modern critical genealogy has identified major flaws in this lineage''':
2 CONT # '''The fictitious parents''': Contemporary Norwegian and Danish medieval historians consider both ''Anna Ranesdatter'' and the specific profile of ''Eyvind Tjostolvsson Bolt'' to be fictional fabrications or highly flawed mixes 
2 CONC of different historical persons.
2 CONT # '''Who was Eivind of Fåle?''' If Thore's wife was indeed a daughter of a man named Eivind from the Fåle estate, this Eivind did not belong to the Bolt family. He was more likely associated with the local elite or the Kusse famil
2 CONC y of the Eiker/Sandsvær region. His exact parentage is lost to history.
2 CONT
2 CONT 🏰 '''The Connection to Elin Ranesdatter and Ulleland'''
2 CONT Despite the lack of proof for her specific parents, the strongest argument for placing her as a sister to Rane Eivindssøn involves property ties:
2 CONT * In 1430, the wealthy noblewoman '''Elin Ranesdatter''' bequeathed the noble seat (''setegård'') of '''Ulleland''' to Thore's son, Jon Thoressøn.
2 CONT * If Thore's wife was indeed the sister of Rane Eivindssøn (making Eivind of Fåle her father), the heir Jon would have been Elin's first cousin.
2 CONT * It is hypothesized that Jon's mother died early (possibly during the Black Death around 1350) and that he grew up with his cousin Elin.
2 CONT * Jon likely died without issue, as six generations later, the Ulleland estate was found in the possession of the descendants of Jon's brother, Reidulf.
2 CONT
2 CONT —————-
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Winther knytter Ukjent Faale  Eivindsdatter som hustru til Thore Reidarssøn. Opplysningene er usikre, men det er grunn til å tro at det fantes en tilknytning mellom den kjente Elin Ranesdatter og og Thores sønn Jon som av hen
2 CONC ne arvet den "adelige sædegaarden" Ulleland på Eker i 1430. Jon må da ha vært en gammel mann. Om dette er riktig kan vi anta at "Ukjent" Eivindsdatter er søster av Hr. Lodin Eivindssøn (Kusse) d1375 (gift med Ingeborg Sigurdsdatte
2 CONC r Kane) og Hr. Rane Eivindssøn gift med Aasa Salmundsdtr på Selvik (død etter 1396). Rane og Aasa var foreldre til Elin Ranesdatter.  "Ukjent" Eivindsdatter døde tidlig, muligens allerede under svartedauen rett før 1350 og sønnen 
2 CONC Jon kan da ha vokst opp sammen med sin kusine Elin Ranesdatter. Jon var muligens uten etterkommere for seks generasjoner senere nevnes Ulleland i eie hos en etterkommer av Jons bror Reidulf.  
