1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.swedenmark.dk/getperson.php?personID=I6000000003349982019&tree=joanmarcussen_dk
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sigrid/Ulfhild (Björnsdotter) / Lakman=
2 CONT Bengt Snivil From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to navigationJump to search Bengt Snivil Issue	Magnus Minniskiöld, Charles the Deaf, Birger Brosa Edit this on Wikidata Father	Folke the Fat Edit this on Wikidata
2 CONT
2 CONT Bengt Snivil (also known as Bengt Snivel) from the House of Bjelbo was a Swedish magnate in mid-12th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some more or less romantic later literature has given him the title of jarl, although no proper historical source attests to such. Romantic genealogies assign a lady Sigrid Lakman as his wife, though without historical source.[cit
2 CONC ation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT Arguably, Bengt Snivil was that Bengt or Benedict, who was son of riksjarl Folke the Fat and Ingegerd Knutsdotter of Denmark, daughter of king Canute IV of Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Bengt Snivil, who thus became an ancestor of important magnates and the future royal family
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Riksjarl Birger Brosa,'''
2 CONT * '''Magnus Minnesköld, father of Birger Jarl,'''
2 CONT * '''Charles the Deaf,''' father of father of jarl Ulf Fase
2 CONT
2 CONT ===FOLKUNGAÄTTEN===
2 CONT
2 CONT Folkungaätten or Bjälboätten are recent names in a medieval Swedish royal family. Some of the agnathic descendants of Bengt Snivil are counted among the Folkungaät. He had three famous sons, Birger, Magnus and Karl. The members of
2 CONC  the family should not be confused with the kings, a group that made several revolts against the king's rule.
2 CONT
2 CONT The genus is usually divided into a number of branches and by Folkungaätt is generally meant the branch that originated from Birger Earl and in a number of generations from and with Birger's son Valdemar Birgersson came to hold th
2 CONC e royal power. For the other branches, see links below.
2 CONT
2 CONT Folkungaätt died out in the late 1300s with Erik Valdemarsson (the younger).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulvhild Bjørnsdtr Sweden was also known as Ulvsdtr. She married Benedikt Folkesen, son of Jarl Folke Ingemunsen Digre and Ingerta Knutsdtr Sweden. She was born at Sweden. She died in Sweden. Benedikt Folkesen was also known as Ben
2 CONC gt Snivil. He married Ulvhild Bjørnsdtr Sweden, daughter of Bjørn Haraldsen Jernside and Katrin Ingesdtr Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
