2 CONT Adela of Meissen
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Adela of Meissen (also Adelheid or Adele) (died 23 October 1181) was a Danish Queen consort, spouse of King Sweyn III of Denmark. She was the daughter of Conrad, Margrave of Meissen, and Luitgard of Ravenstein.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Sweyn in 1152. As queen of Denmark, Adela was not popular, but criticized for influenting her spouse to abandon Danish customs in favour of German ones.
2 CONT
2 CONT Widowed in 1157, she married count Adalbert III of Ballenstedt.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue with Swein
2 CONT
2 CONT Son, died early
2 CONT
2 CONT Luccardis, spouse of Margrave Berthold I of Istria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue with Adalbert
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrudis, spouse of Walther of Arnstein
