1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Świętosława «Gunhilda» Mieszkówna of Poland (Księżniczka polska)=
2 CONT
2 CONT B.Brox: Don't mix her with Sigrid/Sigríð Storråda/the Haughty as several Wikipedia and other sources does.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%9Awi%C4%99tos%C5%82awa_av_Polen
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swiatoslawa_av_Polen
2 CONT
2 CONT Świętosława (967-1014), known in Scandinavian sagas as Gunhild, was Mieszko's I daughter and the sister of the first Polish king Boleslav the Brave. Their mother was probably the Christian wife of Mieszko I, Czech's princess, Dąbr
2 CONC ówka.
2 CONT
2 CONT Świętosława first became a wife of king Erik Segersäll (Eric VI of Sweden) in 980 (or 985), but she became a widow soon.
2 CONT
2 CONT After 994 she married Svend Tveskæg (Sweyn I of Denmark) under the name Gunhild. From the second marriage she probably had five children, including Canute the Great and Harold II of Denmark. Since her marriage was not happy, she r
2 CONC eturned to Poland where her brother Boleslaw the Brave was ruling. After Sweyn died her sons, Kanut and Karald took her back from Poland. Kanut, known as Kanut the Great became later king of England, Denmark and Norway and governo
2 CONC r of Schleswig and Pomerania. She died somewhere in English castle. In any event, Boleslaus I of Poland, the first king of Poland actually sent his troops to help Canute in his successful conquest of England, another sign of close
2 CONC  relationships between Polish rulers and Vikings.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that Świętosława's difficult character was inherited after her aunt Adelaide (Polish Adelajda) who was probably a sister of Mieszko I and also the wife of the Hungarian duke Geza. Adelaide became a mother of St. Stephen
2 CONC  the Great (977-1038), who became the first king of Hungary and a saint.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide was known as a beauty, but she drunk excessively and loved riding horses like a man. Once, she even killed a man in a rage.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.polishsite.us/index.php/history-and-people/middle-ages-and-renaissance/195--swietoslawa-piast-princess-and-vikings-queen-.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/POLAND.htm#MieszkoIdied992
2 CONT
2 CONT --- (soon after 967-).  This is one of the possibilities for the origin of the first wife of Svend I King of Denmark, based solely on Thietmar who refers to the mother of "filiis Suenni" as "Miseconis filia ducis, soror Bolizlavi 
2 CONC successori eius"[69].  Europäische Stammtafeln names her "Šwiętosława [Gunhild] of Poland", although there is no indication of the basis for this suggested Polish name, and states that she married firstly Erik "Segersäll/the Victo
2 CONC rious" King of Sweden, as his second wife[70].  This latter suggestion is implausible as it would mean that both of King Erik's wives were in turn married to Svend King of Denmark, numerous primary sources attesting that the latte
2 CONC r's second wife Sigrid "Storråda/the Haughty" was the widow of King Erik[71].  m ([988/90]) as his first wife, SVEND I "Tveskæg/Forkbeard" King of Denmark, son of HARALD I "Blåtand/Bluetooth" King of Denmark & his first wife Gunhi
2 CONC ld ([960]-Gainsborough 3 Feb 1014, bur in England, later removed to Roskilde).]  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhilda of Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #102419, d. after 1014
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=8 Jul 2005
2 CONT
2 CONT      Gunhilda of Poland is the daughter of Mieszko I, Duke of Poland and Dubrawka of Bohemia. (1) She married Sveyn I 'Forkbeard' Haraldsson, King of Denmark and England, son of Harald I 'Bluetooth' Gormsson, King of Denmark and G
2 CONC yrid Olafsdottir, circa 990. (1) She and Sveyn I 'Forkbeard' Haraldsson, King of Denmark and England were divorced in 1000. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after 1014.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Gunhilda of Poland and Sveyn I 'Forkbeard' Haraldsson, King of Denmark and England
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Gytha Sveynsdottir+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Gunhilda Sveynsdottir 
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. daughter Sveynsdottir+ (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT -4. Santslaue Sveynsdottir (2)
2 CONT
2 CONT -5. Thyra Sveynsdottir b. c 993
2 CONT
2 CONT -6. Harald II Sveynsson, King of Denmark b. c 994, d. bt 1018 - 1019
2 CONT
2 CONT -7. Canute II Sveynsson, King of England and Denmark+ b. c 995, d. 12 Nov 1035
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10242.htm#i102419
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Død efter 2 februar 1014
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild var datter av Kong Burislav Vendeland (Pommen) av Polen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hun var gift med Svein Tjugeskjegg
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn: Harald Sveinsson og Gyda Sveinsdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Død efter 2 februar 1014
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT De sikre informasjoner vi har om Gunhild er ytterst få, hennes slaviske navn er ikke kjent. Adam av Bremen setter hennes ekteskap med Erik Segersäll i forbindelse med et forenet svensk-slavisk angrep på Danmark, men den historiske
2 CONC  bakgrunn for dette kan ikke kontrolleres. Ifølge Adam fødte hun Erik sønnen Olof Skötkonung. Etter Eriks død giftet hun seg med Svend Tjugeskjegg, muligens da denne ca. år 1000 inngikk forbund med kong Olav. Hun ble senere bortvi
2 CONC st av Svend, og levde i mange år i Vendland, inntil hennes sønner etter Svends død hentet henne hjem til Danmark. De islandske sagaforfatterne har knyttet forskjellige ikke historiskt korrekte trekk til hennes navn, og dette har s
2 CONC enere i tradisjonen blitt fortrengt av den svenske dronning Sigrid Storråde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild was the sister of Boleslav I of Poland (992 - 1025) and not his daughter as Snorre Sturlasson related.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: King Olaf Trygvason's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "22. OLAF TRYGVASON'S MARRIAGE.
2 CONT
2 CONT While Olaf lay at Borgundarholm there came on bad weather, storm, and a heavy sea, so that his ships could not lie there; and he sailed southwards under Vindland, where they found a good harbour. They conducted themselves very pea
2 CONC cefully, and remained some time. In Vindland there was then a king called Burizleif, who had three daughters, -- Geira, Gunhild, and Astrid. ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in her life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • She was a Queen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild married Eric VI the Victorious Bjornsson, son of Bjorn the Old of Sweden Ericsson and Unknown, circa 980-985. (Eric VI the Victorious Bjornsson died in 995.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild next married Svend I Haraldsson Tjugeskjegg of Denmark, son of Harald I Gormsson Blåtann of Denmark and Gyrid, circa 995. The marriage ended in divorce in 1000. (Svend I Haraldsson Tjugeskjegg of Denmark was born circa 960
2 CONC , died on 3 Feb 1014 in Gainsborough, Lincolnshire, England and was buried in Roskilde Cathedral, Denmark 4.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Død efter 2 februar 1014
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen Swietoslava of Sweden Norway & Denmark - also known as: Sygryda - was born about 0970, lived in Poznan, Poznan, Poland and died after 2 Feb 1014 . She was the daughter of Prince Mieszko I of Poland and Princess Dubravka of B
2 CONC ohemia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen Swietoslava married King Erik VIII Bjornsson "Victorious" of Sweden about 0985. King Erik was born about 0930, lived in Sweden. He was the son of King Bjorn Eriksson "the Old" of Sweden. He died in 0994/0995 in Uppsala, Upps
2 CONC ala, Sweden . 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Then Queen Swietoslava married King Svend I "Forked Beard" of Denmark, Norway & England in 0998. King Svend was born about 0960, lived in Denmark. He died on 2 Feb 1014 in Gainsborough, Lincolnshire, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Flyttad till Roskilde domkyrka i Danmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Noteringar 
2 CONT
2 CONT Polsk prinsessa, drottning av Danmark, Norge och England
2 CONT
2 CONT Att Sven Tveskägg var gift med en polsk prinsessa är bevisat (Gunhild, dotter av Mieszko I) Enligt källor jag har stött på var Sven gift både med Gunhild av Polen och Sigrid Storråda. Många hävdar dock att de är en och samma perso
2 CONC n, så jag redovisar tills vidare Gunhild som moder till Estrid. Frågan är då om denna Gunhild även är mor till Olof Skötkonung.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage (1): Eric VI the Victorious Bjornsson circa 980-985 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage (2): Svend I Haraldsson Tjugeskjegg of Denmark circa 995
2 CONT
2 CONT  General Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT De sikre informasjoner vi har om Gunhild er ytterst få, hennes slaviske navn er ikke kjent. Adam av Bremen setter hennes ekteskap med Erik Segersäll i forbindelse med et forenet svensk-slavisk angrep på Danmark, men den historiske
2 CONC  bakgrunn for dette kan ikke kontrolleres. Ifølge Adam fødte hun Erik sønnen Olof Skötkonung. Etter Eriks død giftet hun seg med Svend Tjugeskjegg, muligens da denne ca. år 1000 inngikk forbund med kong Olav. Hun ble senere bortvi
2 CONC st av Svend, og levde i mange år i Vendland, inntil hennes sønner etter Svends død hentet henne hjem til Danmark. De islandske sagaforfatterne har knyttet forskjellige ikke historiskt korrekte trekk til hennes navn, og dette har s
2 CONC enere i tradisjonen blitt fortrengt av den svenske dronning Sigrid Storråde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild was the sister of Boleslav I of Poland (992 - 1025) and not his daughter as Snorre Sturlasson related.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: King Olaf Trygvason's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "22. OLAF TRYGVASON'S MARRIAGE.
2 CONT
2 CONT While Olaf lay at Borgundarholm there came on bad weather, storm, and a heavy sea, so that his ships could not lie there; and he sailed southwards under Vindland, where they found a good harbour. They conducted themselves very pea
2 CONC cefully, and remained some time. In Vindland there was then a king called Burizleif, who had three daughters, -- Geira, Gunhild, and Astrid. ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT   Noted events in her life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • She was a Queen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild married Eric VI the Victorious Bjornsson, son of Bjorn the Old of Sweden Ericsson and Unknown, circa 980-985. (Eric VI the Victorious Bjornsson died in 995.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild next married Svend I Haraldsson Tjugeskjegg of Denmark, son of Harald I Gormsson Blåtann of Denmark and Gyrid, circa 995. The marriage ended in divorce in 1000. (Svend I Haraldsson Tjugeskjegg of Denmark was born circa 960
2 CONC , died on 3 Feb 1014 in Gainsborough, Lincolnshire, England and was buried in Roskilde Cathedral, Denmark 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT " OLAF TRYGVASON'S MARRIAGE.
2 CONT
2 CONT While Olaf lay at Borgundarholm there came on bad weather, storm, and a heavy sea, so that his ships could not lie there; and he sailed southwards under Vindland, where they found a good harbour. They conducted themselves very pea
2 CONC cefully, and remained some time. In Vindland there was then a king called Burizleif, who had three daughters, -- Geira, Gunhild, and Astrid. ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a Queen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild married Eric VI the Victorious Bjornsson, son of Bjorn the Old of Sweden Ericsson and Unknown, circa 980-985. (Eric VI the Victorious Bjornsson died in 995.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhild next married Svend I Haraldsson Tjugeskjegg of Denmark, son of Harald I Gormsson Blåtann of Denmark and Gyrid, circa 995. The marriage ended in divorce in 1000. (Svend I Haraldsson Tjugeskjegg of Denmark was born circa 960
2 CONC , died on 3 Feb 1014 in Gainsborough, Lincolnshire, England and was buried in Roskilde Cathedral, Denmark)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhilda married Eric VI 'the Victorious' Björnsson, son of Björn 'the Old' Ericsson, about 980-985.1 (Eric VI 'the Victorious' Björnsson died in 995 1.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunhilda next married Sveyn I 'Forkbeard' Haraldsson King of Denmark about 995.1 2 (Sveyn I 'Forkbeard' Haraldsson King of Denmark was born about 960,2 died on 3 Feb 1014 in Gainsborough, Lincolnshire, England 2 and was buried in 
2 CONC Roskilde Cathedral, Copenhagen, Denmark 2.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  1 Lundy, Darryl, "The Peerage.com - A Genealogical Survey of the Peerage of England as well as the Royal Families of Europe" (http://www.thepeerage.com rev. 12 Mar 2006), Citing: Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Ge
2 CONC nealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 24-26. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2  I Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==========================
2 CONT
2 CONT Have FOund the wife listed at one time as
2 CONT
2 CONT PRINCE OBOTRITES MIECESLAS was born 919.  He married SOPHIA [-?-] .  She was born Abt. 921. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child is: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ASTRID OR INEGRID, PSS. OF OBOTRITES, b. Abt. 979, Sweden;married III OLAF, KING OF SWEDEN son of VIII ERIK and QUEEN SKOGLAR-TESTEDOTTER.  He was born Abt. 950 in Sweden, and died 1022."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT It is said that she was the mother of Knud den Store, who was born ab. 995. At that point her brother Boleslaw is 29 and Swietoslawa is 28 years. After Sven Tveskæg's death in 1014, Knud and Harald fetched their mother in Slavia, 
2 CONC which might mean that she had gone home to her brother Boleslaw. The brothers buried their father's body - which had been brought to Denmark "by a certain English lady" - in the church he had let build in Roskilde. According to a 
2 CONC note Boleslaw helped ab. 1015 Knud den Store (his nephew) with a detachment of Polish horsemen, when he went to England with his army to claim the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT This is one of the possibilities for the origin of the first wife of Svend I King of Denmark, based solely on Thietmar who refers to the mother of "filiis Suenni" as "Miseconis filia ducis, soror Bolizlavi successori eius” [Thietm
2 CONC ar VII.39, p. 334.].  Europäische Stammtafeln names her "Šwiętosława [Gunhild] of Poland", although there is no indication of the basis for this suggested Polish name, and states that she married firstly Erik "Segersäll/the Victor
2 CONC ious" King of Sweden, as his second wife [ES II 114 and 120.].  This latter suggestion is implausible as it would mean that both of King Erik's wives were in turn married to Svend King of Denmark, numerous primary sources attestin
2 CONC g that the latter's second wife Sigrid "Storråda/the Haughty" was the widow of King Erik [For example, Laing, S. (trans.) (1907) Snorri Sturluson, Heimskringla: A History of the Norse Kings Snorre (Norroena Society, London), King 
2 CONC Olav Trygvason's Saga Part III, 98, available at Online Medieval and Classical Library Release 15b, http://sunsite.berkeley.edu/OMACL/Heimskringla/ (24 Jan 2003).].
2 CONT --------------------
