2 CONC rn, king of Sweden.[citation needed] Styrbjorn's wife, Thyra Haraldsdotter,[citation needed] was the daughter of Harold Bluetooth (king of Denmark and Norway). However, this pedigree may have been concocted to glorify his descenda
2 CONC nts, who later reigned in Denmark. Alternatively, Saxo Grammaticus reports he was son of a bear.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at the Battle of Swold.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were Ulf (d. 1027), the Earl of Canute the Great in Denmark and Danish steward, and Gytha Thorkelsdóttir who was to marry Godwin, Earl of Wessex.[citation needed]
