1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = SVERKER II "den yngre/the younger" King of Sweden=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of King Charles VII Sverkersson of Sweden and Queen Christina Hvide 
2 CONT * He succeeded in 1196 as SVERKER II "den yngre/the younger" King of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sverker was a son of King Karl Sverkersson of Sweden and Queen Christine Stigsdatter of Hvide, a Danish noblewoman. Through his mother, he was a cousin's son of the Danish kings Canute VI and Valdemar Sejr. His parents' marriage
2 CONC  has been dated to 1162 or more probably 1163.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#SverkerIIdied1210 KINGS of SWEDEN - FAMILY of SVERKER]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Project MedLands Sweden'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SVERKER''', son of --- (-murdered 24/25 Dec 1156).  Sverker's parentage is not known.  According to Saxo Grammaticus, he was "of modest origins"[122].  Under King in Östergötland.  He was installed as '''SVERKER I King of Swede
2 CONC n in [1133/34] in succession to Magnus Nielsson of Denmark. '''married firstly as her third husband, ULVHILD Haakonsdotter,''' widow first of INGE II Halstensson King of Sweden and secondly of NIELS King of Denmark, daughter of HA
2 CONC AKON Finsson & his wife --- (-before 1143).'''  Her second marriage is referred to by Saxo Grammaticus who states that "Ulvildam Noricam", wife of "Nicolaus", was secretly abducted by King Sverker but their "connection was accepte
2 CONC d as a marriage"[123].  Fagrskinna names “Úlfhildr dróttning, dóttir Hákonar Finnssunar Hárekssunar or Þjóttu” as mother of “Karl konungs”, adding that she had first married “Nikolás Danakonungr”, secondly “Ingi Sviakonungr Hallst
2 CONC einssunr” and thirdly “Sverkir konungr Kolssunr”[124]. '''married secondly (after 1143) as her third husband, RYKSA Swantosława of Poland,''' widow firstly of MAGNUS I "den Stærke/the Strong" King of Denmark and secondly of [VOLOD
2 CONC AR], daughter of BOLESŁAW III "Krzywousty/Wrymouth" Prince of Poland & his second wife Salome von Berg-Schelklingen ([1116/17]-after 25 Dec 1155).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Rikissam" as the only daughter 
2 CONC of "dux Vergescelaus de Polonia" and his wife Agnes, specifying that "primo fuit regina Suecie", that by her second husband "regi Russie nomine Musuch" she was mother of "Sophiam reginam Dacie et Rikissam", the latter marrying "im
2 CONC peratoris Castelle Alfunso"[125].  This appears to be a confused account which contradicts other sources in many aspects.  She was known as RIKISSA in Sweden.  Her third marriage is confirmed by Knytlíngasaga which records that [h
2 CONC er son] “Knúti konúngi” fled to ”Sörkvir konúngr átti Rikizu, módur Þeirra Knúts konúngs ok Súffiu” after being defeated by King Svend III[126].  The marriage is also confirmed by the Liber Census Daniæ which records that the esta
2 CONC te of [her son by King Sverker] “Bulizlaus” was inherited by his sister Sofia Queen of Denmark [Ryksa’s daughter by her second husband][127]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Sverker I & his first wife ULVHILD Haakonsdotter had four children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''JOHAN Sverkersson''' (-murdered [1153/54]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He appears to have been his father's designated heir but was killed (by peasants?) some yea
2 CONC rs before his father's death[128].   
2 CONT * 2.         '''KARL Sverkersson''' (-murdered Visingsö 12 Apr [1166], bur Alvastra Abbey).  His parentage is stated by Saxo Grammaticus[129].  '''He succeeded in 1161 as KARL I King of Sweden.'''  '''married (1163) KRISTIN Stigsd
