2 CONT Also known as Charles the Deaf (Swedish: Karl Döve) from the House of Bjelbo
2 CONT
2 CONT * KARL .  “Byrgerus dux magnus et Karolus fratres eius” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/85] under which “Kanutus…Rex Sweorum atque Gotthorum” donated property to the monks of Juleta kloster[36].  “Byrgo Sweorum et Guttorum dux…
2 CONC Philippus frater meus, Magnus et Karolus fratres ducis…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “K…Sweorum rex filius Herjcjs itjdem regis” donated property to Nydala kloster 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Swedish Nobility- https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDISH%20NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Charles the Deaf (Swedish: Karl Döve) from the House of Bjelbo==
2 CONT
2 CONT Was the jarl of Sweden during 1216–1220. His father was magnate Bengt Snivil. He was the brother of Magnus Minnesköld and jarl Birger Brosa and father of jarl Ulf Fase. Charles died at the Battle of Lihula in Estonia August 8, 122
2 CONC 0.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The seal of Charles, discovered in the early 1990s, is dated to the end of the 12th century and thus the oldest preserved personal object in Swedish history. Personal seals were normally broken to pieces at the death of the owner 
2 CONC in order to prevent later abuse, and the intact seal of Charles is therefore unique.[2] The Swedish Museum of National Antiquities bought it in 2001 for SEK 800,000
2 CONT
2 CONT N Ahnlund, Vreta monastery's oldest donors (HT 1945), p 340; S Bolin, Folkungarna (Sc 1935), pp. 227, 232; W M Carlgren, About Finland's Relationships with Sweden and the Pope 1216–1237 (HT 1950), p 257 f; S Carlsson, Folkungarna 
2 CONC (PHT 1953); DS 1 (1829); H Gillingstam, rec of S O Brenner, Gorm the Old Descendants (PHT 1967); K G Grandinson, Narke's Medieval Records, 1 (1935); Hakonar saga (1887); Heinrich's Livländische Chronik (1955); H Jägerstad, Court d
2 CONC ay and advice during the Middle Ages (1948); K H K [arlsson], Folkungaätten (SAT 1, 1879-88); Å Ljungfors, Contribution to Swedish diplomacy before 1350 (1955), p 152 f, 212 f; G Paulsson, Annales suecici medii aevi (1974); ST 1 (
2 CONC 1877), s 132 f; P Stensland, Julita Monastery's Freight Policy (1945)., P 14; K B Westman, The Evolution of the Swedish Church from St. Bernhard's Age to Innocent III's (1915), pp. 229, 264, 278; K G Westman, Swedish Council Histo
2 CONC ry to the Year 1306 (1904), p 6; J Ödberg, Royal Chancellor and Diplomatics in Sweden until about 1250 (1974), Hans Gillingstam
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl oli yearly and Birger Brosan veli sek Birger yearly set. Hands on Folkunga-suvun jäsen. Jarl (Earl) Carl Carlsen Døve Died in 1220 in Sweden (Sweden). Jarl Carl Carlsen Døve was born at Sweden. He was a crusader, Earl. He die
2 CONC d in 1220 at Sweden.
2 CONT
