1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dobrawa_Przemy%C5%9Blidka Dobrawa w Wikipedii po Polsku]
2 CONT
2 CONT 	 [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dobrawa_of_Bohemia Dobrawa on Wikipedia in English]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dobrawa (Czech: Doubravka) was a Bohemian princess member of the Přemyslid dynasty and by marriage Duchess of the Polans. According to earlier sources she urged her husband to accept the baptism in 966. However, modern historians 
2 CONC believed that the change of religion by Mieszko I was one of the points discussed in the Polish-Bohemian agreement performed soon before his marriage with Dobrawa, whose role in the conversion of her husband is now considered wasn
2 CONC 't so important as it's represented by the medieval chronicles.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
