2 CONT Main
2 CONT
2 CONT duke (from 992) and then (from 1024) first king of Poland, who expanded his country’s territory to include Pomerania, Lusatia, and, for a time, the Bohemian princely lands. He made Poland a major European state and also created a 
2 CONC Polish church independent of German control.
