1 NOTE Boleslav I the Brave - of Poland - united Moravia and Poland in year 1000
2 CONT and persuaded Otto III Holy Roman Emperor to create independent bishopric
2 CONT for Bohemia at Gnesen.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the year 1000, during the reign of Boleslav I, he consolidated and extended his kingdom of Poland in all directions.  There was an archiepiscopal see established at Gniezno.
2 CONT Boleslav/Boleslaw had overrun Pomerania, Silesia, Moravia, the Kiev region of Russian, as well as others.  But, at his death in 1025, his son Mieszko II managed to lose most of this territory.  The danes captured Pomerania.  The r
2 CONC ussians regained Kiev, and the Czechs gained their independence.
1 NOTE aka Chobry (Chrobny) PIAST; `der Tapfere' le brave
1 NOTE Data From Lynn Jeffrey Bernhard, 2445 W 450 South #4, Springville UT  84663-4950 
