2 CONC n Sachsen in Ratzeburg und Lauenburg. ERICH von Sachsen, son of JOHANN I Herzog von Sachsen, Engern und Westfalen & his wife Ingeborg of Sweden (-Nienburg 1361).  The Annales Lubicenses name (in order) "Alberti, Iohannis et Erici 
2 CONC ducum Saxoniæ" as sons of "Ingeburgis…filia Regis Sweonum"[679].  “Albertus...Saxoniæ, Angariæ, Westphaliæ dux, comes de Bren, burgraviusque Magdeburg...cum domina Elizabet quondam comitissa in Bren sorore nostra” confirmed donati
2 CONC ons made to Kloster Coswick by “filius eius Albertus piæ recordationis”, with the consent of “fratruelium nostrorum Johannis, Alberti et Erici et filiorum nostrorum Rudolphi et Alberti”, by charter dated 16 Mar 1293[680].  He succ
2 CONC eeded in 1305 as ERICH I Herzog von Sachsen in Ratzeburg und Lauenburg.  Subdeacon and canon at Magdeburg Cathedral 1306/1308. '''married  (1316 before 16 Jun, Papal dispensation 3o 1 Jul 1346) ELISABETH von Pommern,''' daughter o
2 CONC f BOGISLAW IV Duke of Pomerania in Wolgast & his second wife Margareta von Rügen (-after 16 Oct 1349).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Erike de erste, Hertoghe Johannes sone to Sassen” married “Elizabeth
2 CONC  des Hertoghen dochter to Stettyn”[681]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Project MedLands Saxony Dukes 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Chapter 3.    KINGS of SWEDEN 1250-1412 (FOLKINGAÄTTEN)==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIRGER Magnusson, son of MAGNUS "Minnesköld" [Folkungaätten] & his second wife Ingrid [Ylva] ([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).'''  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in Sv
2 CONC ecia" in 1248[173].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founder of Stockholm.  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj
2 CONC  ac Benedictj Scolaris”[174].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1265 of "Birgerus dux Sveciæ"[175]. '''married firstly ([1235]) INGEBORG of Sweden, daughter of ERIK Knutsson King of Sweden & his second wife Richeza of Denm
2 CONC ark ([1212]-17 Jun 1254)'''.  Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 4 Nov 1246 in which “Ericus…rex Swethie” names “domino Birgero genero nostro”[176].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified
2 CONC .  '''married secondly (1261) as her second husband, MECHTILD von Holstein, widow of ABEL King of Denmark, daughter of ADOLF IV Graf von Holstein und Stormarn & his wife Hedwig zur Lippe (1225-1288, bur Varnhem Abbey).'''  The Ann
2 CONC ales Stadenses record the marriage "1237 VII Kal Mai" of "dux Abel" and "filiam comitis Adolfi de Scowenborch", naming her "Mechtildem" and recording her second marriage to "ducem Sueciæ" in a later passage[177].  The Icelandic An
2 CONC nals record the marriage in 1261 of "Bergerus Sveciæ dux" and "Mathildam reginam Daniæ"[178].  '''Mistress (1): ---.  The name of Birger's mistress is not known.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson & his first wife INGEBORG of Sweden had eight children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''RIKISSA Birgersdotter''' (-before 13 Dec 1288).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Rixam filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Henricum seniorem [filium Nycolai domini de Werle]"[179].  The primary source which confi
2 CONC rms her first marriage has not yet been identified.  m firstly (Oslo 1251) HAAKON Haakonsson "den Unge/the Young" under King of Norway, son of HAAKON IV "den Gamle/the Old" King of Norway & his wife Margareta Skulesdotter (Bergen 
2 CONC 10 Nov 1232-Tønsberg 30 Apr or 5 May1257, bur Oslo, St Hallvards Church).  m secondly (1262) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Werle, son of NIKOLAUS I Herr von Werle zu Rostock [Mecklenburg] & his wife Jutta von Anhalt (-murdered n
2 CONC ear Saal, Rügen 8 Oct 1291).  Herr zu Werle zu Güstrow 1281. 
2 CONT * 2.         '''VALDEMAR Birgersson''' ([1237]-Nyköping Castle 26 Dec 1302).  The Icelandic Annals record that "Valdemarus Birgiri filius" succeeded as king of Sweden in 1249[180].  He succeeded in 1250 as VALDEMAR King of Sweden.
2 CONC   “Waldemarus…rex Swechie” confirmed the donation of property to Gudhems Kloster by “reginam dominam Katerinam” by charter dated 17 Jan 1251 which names “patris nostri domini Byrgerj ducis”[181].  The Annales Lubicenses records th
2 CONC at "Waldemarus rex Sweorum" was deposed in 1275 by "Magno duce fratre suo"[182].  The Icelandic Annals record the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus" and the departure of Valdemar for Denmark soon after[183].  The I
2 CONC celandic Annals record the death in 1302 of "Valdemarus Birgeri filius Rex Sveonum"[184].  ''''married  firstly (1260, divorced after 1276) SOPHIE of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife Jutta of S
2 CONC axony (-1286).'''  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[185].  The Icelandic Annals note the presenc
2 CONC e of "Sophia regina Valdimari regis, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[186].  '
2 CONC ''married secondly LUCARDIS, daughter of ---.  1296.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.'''   '''Mistress (1): JUTTA of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife
2 CONC  Jutta of Saxony ([1246]-[1286/95]).'''  Abbess of St Agneta in Roskilde 1266.  She left the convent in 1271[187]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' King Valdemar had & his first wife SOPHIE of Denmark had seven children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' (-1261, bur Sigruna Abbey).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT >>>>* b)        ''' INGEBORG Valdemarsdotter''' (-[1290]).  The Annales Lubicenses refer to the first wife of "Gherardi comitis Holtzatiæ" as "filia Woldemari Regis Sweciæ"[188].  “Waldemarus…Rex Sveorum” confirmed a grant to Hamb
2 CONC urg by “pater noster Dominus Byrgerus felicis memoriæ Dux Sveorum” by charter dated 12 Dec 1275 “in nuptiis filiæ nostræ…et comitis Gerardi…de Holsatia”[189].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence of "Sophia regina Valdimari reg
2 CONC is, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[190].  '''married  (12 Dec 1275) as his f
2 CONC irst wife, GERHARD II Graf von Holstein in Plön, son of GERHARD I Graf von Holstein in Itzehoe & his first wife Elisabeth von Mecklenburg (1254-Plön 28 Oct 1312, bur Hamburg Cathedral).'''
2 CONT >>>>* c)         '''KATARINA Valdemarsdotter''' (-1283).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[191].
2 CONC
2 CONT >>>>* d)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' [Folkungaättens Valdemarsgren] ([1271/72]-1330).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico 
2 CONC annos quinque nato" in 1276[192].  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[193].  The Icelandic Annals 
2 CONC record that "domicellus Ericus filius Valdemari" was released from prison in 1302[194].  Norwegian High Councillor 1308.  Swedish High Councillor 1322.  '''married  INGEBORG Knutsdotter, daughter of KNUT Jonsson [Aspenäsätten] & h
2 CONC is wife Katharina Bengtsdotter [Folkungaättens lagmansgren] 1333.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Erik & his wife INGEBORG Knutsdotter had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* i)          '''VALDEMAR Eriksson''' 1345/69.  '''married firstly (before 1347) INGEGÄRD Karlsdotter [Färla],''' daughter of [KARL Orestason [Färla] & his wife Helena Magnusdotter [Folkungaättens oäkta gren]].  '''married s
2 CONC econdly as her first husband, HELGA Anundsdotter [Balk av Strand],''' daughter of ANUND Röriksson [Balk av Strand] & his wife Cecilia Magnusdotter.  She married secondly (before 1379) Ya Königsmarck, Vogt of Stockholm Castle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Valdemar & his wife had one child:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* (a)       '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' (-[1388/96]).  married  ERMEGARD--- (-[1402/03].
2 CONT >>>>* e)         '''RIKISSA Valdemarsdotter''' (-[1 Sep 1288/19 Apr 1293]).  The Annales Polonorum record the marriage "1285 in octavis sancti Francisci" of "filiam regis Swecie nomine Rithcam" and "dux Primislius maioris Polonie"
2 CONC [195].  '''married  (1285) as his second wife, PRZEMYSŁ Prince of Greater Poland, son of PRZEMYSŁ I Prince of Poznan, Kalisch and Gniezien [Piast] & his wife Elisabeth von Schlesien [Piast]''' (14 Oct 1257-murdered Rogoźno 8 Feb 1
2 CONC 296, bur Posen Cathedral).  He succeeded in 1295 as PRZEMYSŁ II King of Poland. 
2 CONT >>>>* f)          '''MARIANNA Valdemarsdotter'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   1299.  '''married  (Nyköping 1285) as his second wife, RUDOLF von Diepholz, son of --- (
2 CONC -1303 or after).'''
2 CONT >>>>* g)         '''MARGARETA Valdemarsdotter'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.   Nun at Skänninge Convent 1288. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Valdemar had one possible illegitimate son by Mistress (1): JUTTA of Denmark'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* h)         '''ERIK Valdemarsson''' ([1273]-).  Brenner doubts his existence, saying he is likely confused with King Valdemar's legitimate son Erik[196].] 
2 CONT * 3.         '''MAGNUS Ladulås Birgersson''' ([1240]-Visingsö 18 Dec 1290, bur Stockholm, Riddarholm Church).  The Annales Lubicenses names "Magno duce fratre suo [=Waldemarus rex Sweorum]" when recording that he deposed his broth
2 CONC er in 1275[197].  He succeeded in 1275 as MAGNUS I Ladulås King of Sweden.   
2 CONT * 4.         '''KRISTINA Birgersdotter''' (-after 1285).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   '''married SIGGE Guttormsson, from Ljuna''' (-bur Alvastra Abbey).
2 CONT * 5.         '''KATARINA  Birgersdotter,'''  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Katerinam, filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Sifridum comitem"[198].  '''married  (before 17 Oct 1259) SIEGFRIED Graf von Anhalt in Köthen und Dessau
2 CONC , son of HEINRICH I "der Fette" Graf von Anhalt und Aschersleben & his wife Irmgard von Thüringen (-after 25 Mar 1298, bur Coswig).'''
2 CONT * 6.         '''ERIK Birgersson,''' (-17 Dec 1275).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolaris”[199
2 CONC ].  Duke in southern Sweden 1275. 
2 CONT * '''7.         INGEBORG (-30 Jun 1302, bur Mölln).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie refers to the wife of "Iohannem [filium Alberti dux]" as "filiam regis Suecie"[200].  The Annales Lubicenses record the death in 1302 of "Ingeburgi
2 CONC s, mater Alberti, Iohannis et Erici ducum Saxoniæ, filia Regis Sweonum"[201].  married  ([1270]) JOHANN I Herzog von Sachsen, son of ALBRECHT I Herzog zu Sachsen, Engern und Westfalen [Askanier] & his third wife Helene von Braunsc
2 CONC hweig (-30 Jul 1286).'''
2 CONT * 8.         '''BENGT Birgersson''' ([1254]-25 May 1291).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolari
2 CONC s”[202].  Duke in Finland 1284.  Bishop of Linköping 1286. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson had one illegitimate son by Mistress (1):'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 9.          '''GREGERS Birgersson''' or Frilloson [Folkingaättens oäkta gren] (-1276, bur Uppsala).  At Ängsjö.  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1276 of "Gregorius filius notus Birgeri comitis"[203].  He was ancestor of
2 CONC  the Folkingaättens Oäkta Gren family. 
