1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Eskil Magnusson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Magnus Bengtsson Minnesköld (Folkungaätten) and N.N. Karlsdotter ( Spekulativ ana )
2 CONT * Eskil Magnusson (c. 1175 – c. 1227) was a nobleman and lawspeaker (Lagmän) of Västergötland. He is the first attested legal official in what is now Sweden about whom we have any extensive information.
2 CONT * Eskil Magnusson ( lion) (Folkungaätten, son of Magnus Minnesköld at Bjälbo. Lagman ca 1217 and died ca 1227)
2 CONT * Eskil Magnusson , born about 1170 - 1175 and died about 1227 , was the son of Magnus Minnisköld in his first known marriage and thus half-brother of Birger Earl . He married about 1217 with Kristina Nilsdotter Blake , who was th
2 CONC e daughter of Erik the Holy and widow of the Norwegian Earl Hakon crazy.
2 CONT * He was a member of the Bjelbo dynasty or House of Folkung (Folkungaätten) which in the 1250s became Sweden's royal dynasty. He was the son of Magnus Minniskiöld, and the elder half-brother of Birger Jarl (Birger Magnusson), the 
2 CONC most powerful man of Sweden in the middle of the 13th century.
2 CONT * Eskil Magnusson appears in written documents at the end of Knut Eriksson's reign. He was a teammate in Västergötland at the latest from 1217. According to the Västgötalagen's teammate's length , Eskil was a writer for the Västgö
2 CONC talagen . During the first year of the 1220s, he participated in negotiations with the Norwegian king Håkon Håkonsson regarding the Ribbungar's use of Värmland as a base area for looting trains into Norway.
2 CONT * The banner that King Erik Knutsson of Sweden carried at the Battle of Gestilren was stored at Eskil Magnusson in Skara, which in 1219 handed it as a gift of honor to the visiting Icelandic lawman Snorre Sturlasson .
2 CONT * Eskil was noted for his learning and seems to have had an important role in codifying the law of Västergötland, (Västgötalagen) the oldest known Swedish text written in the Latin script.[7] The list of lawspeakers of Västergötla
2 CONC nd appended to Västgötalagen tells that he collected and edited the province's laws, and administered justice with great consideration. He had good judgment, the learning of a cleric and he was superior to all the chieftains of th
2 CONC e kingdom. The list also claims that he distinguished himself in bravery and that it would take a long time until another man of that kind was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003353135037?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000138140505851 '''Kristina Nikolausdotter,'''] daughter of Nikolaus Blake and Katarina Eriksdtr Sverige, in 1214. He was Lagmann
2 CONC  in 1220. Around 1217, he married Kristina Nilsdotter, widow of the Norwegian earl Hakon the Mad (Håkon Galen), whose son Knut Håkonsson was a pretender to the Norwegian throne. Due to the location of his jurisdiction and his marr
2 CONC iage to Kristina, Eskil had good contacts in Norway and may have functioned as a negotiator between the Swedish and the Norwegian monarchs. Some time during 1218–1220, he was visited by Icelandic historian Snorri Sturluson.
2 CONT
2 CONT =[http://www.theutenberg.se/pdf/Tornetaggen.pdfFolk Kid Eskil Magnusson (lion)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Folk kid Eskil Magnusson (lion) was Västergötland's layman from about 1217 to about 1227. The names Algot and Sigtrygg indicate, as I said, in connection with Västergötland's oldest lawyers. The name Algot includes the element - g
2 CONC aut (gautigoth), the term for ingots, ingots. It is an important fact that the elders of the gutters, or gutters, bore the name Al-gaut. As mentioned at the outset, in Snorre Sturlason's Yngling saga, a king Algaut of Gautland, ie
2 CONC  Götaland, is mentioned. It was Ingjald Illråde who became the wife of King Algauts daughter Gauthild (Göthild). Snorre says of Ingjald's bride: "It was Gauthild, daughter of King Algaut; he was the son of King Gautrek the gentle,
2 CONC  son the first half of the century designations on the descendants of Folkes and Ingegärd.
2 CONT
2 CONT to Gaut, after which Gautland has been named ”. All these names refer to Götaland and the trail -got, -göt. In the sagas of Heimskringlas Magnus Lagabøtes, Västergötland's teammate Algot is mentioned Brynolfsson under the name Alg
2 CONC aute Brynjolvsson. Here we talk about the disputes which led to Duke Magnus Birgersson (Ladulås) deposing his brother king in 1275 Valdemar Birgersson. In this context, a conciliation board was appointed, ken, ”Heimskringla says, 
2 CONC included the teammate 'Algaute Brynjolvsson', 'Jon Filippusson ',' Ulv Karlsson ', nephew of Earl Ulf Fase, and' Marshal Karl '. Here meets interesting names, namely Ulf Karlsson (winged arrowhead) and his uncle
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Ulf Fase (lion), descendants of Earl Karl Döve (embroidery in his shield), and also Johan Filipsson of Aspenäsätt (lion eagle) and Marshal Karl Gustavsson (two syllables in other crosses). The latter two were close to King Ma
2 CONC gnus Birgersson, but still participated with life and desire in the rebellion against him. This cost Johan Philip the head, while Marshal Karl succeeded in reconciling himself with the king (see table24)
2 CONT
2 CONT The lawyer Algot Brynolfsson, probably in his only known marriage with Margareta Petersdotter (troll lion) - the lawyer Peter Näfs (lion) daughter - the sons Brynolf, Magnus, Karl, Folke, Bengt, Peter, Rörik and Nils. It is Brynol
2 CONC f's son who in 1278 is elected bishop of Skara diocese, and it is this Brynolf Algotsson who King Magnus Birgersson's (Ladulås) brother Duke Bengt Birgersson in a letter 1277 (DS 621) mentions his consanguineus, that is his blood 
2 CONC relative. These common names Bengt, Magnus and Folke also indicate a relationship with Folkungaätten. Magnus Minnesköld on Bjälbo was the son of Bengt Snivels and grandson of Folke the thick and his Danish wife the king's daughter
2 CONC  Ingegerd Knutsdotter (King Knut the holy daughter). The proven blood ties between Bishop Brynolf Algotsson and Duke Bengt Birgersson suggest fairly unequivocally that Västergötland's lion-carrying lawman Peter Näf was a descendan
2 CONC t of West Gothic lawman Eskil Magnusson (lion), one of Magnus Minneskölds (trol lion) at Bjälbo , not to say the oldest. Lawman Peter Näf must therefore have been Bishop Brynolf Algotsson's grandfather. As is clear from the geneal
2 CONC ogical tables, the same Magnus Minnesköld on Bjälbo was Duke Bengt Birgersson's grandfather. It should be remembered that there is a significant temporal shift between Magnus Minnesköld's probably eldest son Västergötland's teamma
2 CONC te Eskil Magnusson (lion) and the youngest son Birger Jarl Magnusson (lion), Duke Bengt Birgersson's (lion) father.  As illustrated above, it is the so-called Vidhems priest (Vidhem is now called Vedum) who, in his length over Väs
2 CONC tergötland's lawmakers, gives some information about the lawyer Eskil Magnusson (lion), who was the lawman over Västergöt-land from about 1217 to 1227 (see picture no. 2).  wäghä wäl suited to this walz. He had God-given that he w
2 CONC ould be kind to others man .... And in all his courage he strengthened his way and their court. He was a Magnusiansun Minniskiolz by Bialbo ”. Thus: “He was in many ways well sent for this acquisition. He had the gift of God, that
2 CONC  he had a sharp mind, more than others men ... And in everything he supported the Western Goths and their chiefs. He was the son of another Magnus Memorial Shield by Bjälbo ”. It should be noted that the length of the team speaks 
2 CONC of “western the gutters and their chieftains ”. tergötland. It is probable that these chiefs were to be found in the arches or royal farms ("Husabyar" and "Tuna resorts"), which belonged to the so-called Uppsala 25
2 CONT
2 CONT The first editorial board of the Older Västgötalagen is put in conjunction with teammate Eskil Magnusson, son of Magnus Minnesköld at Bjälbo in Östergötland and grandson's son of Folke den Tjocke and Danish royal daughter Ingegerd
2 CONC  Knutsdotter. Åke Holmbäck and Elias Wessén say in the Swedish Landscaping Act that teamman Eskil seems to have been born around 1175 and that during his youth he spent some time at King Knut Eriksson's court. During this time he 
2 CONC has also acquired thorough knowledge, which according to the length of the team was to equate with good clerks. Lagman Eskil's name may give rise to associations as to where this name could originate according to the principle of 
2 CONC calling. It should also be able to give some guidance on who was Team Eskil's mother, ie Magnus Minneskölds on Bjälbo's first wife. The chronological conditions for Magnus Minnesköld's children presuppose that before his marriage 
2 CONC to Birger Jarl Magnusson's mother Ingrid Ylva, he had a first marriage, in which Magnus Minnesköld's older child must be born.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably, teammate Eskil Magnusson descended on the mother from Götajarlen Erik
2 CONT If you summarize what Saxo has to say and imply in this matter, which is supported by Finnish historian Jarl Gallén in his 1985 article on Knut the Holy and Adela of Flanders, Magnus Minnesköld's first wife may have been a daughte
2 CONC r of the Nordic primate, the Danish Archbishop Eskil in Lund, who was born about 1100 and died in 1181. As prelate as he was, he had a daughter, who married Karl Eriksson whom Saxo mentions as Earl of Halland around the year 1152.
2 CONC  The birth of his daughter should have occurred before Eskil became bishop of Roskilde in 1134. Jarlen Karl Eriksson and his wife NN Eskilsdotter had at least 1176 sons Knut Karlsson and Karl Karlsson. So there would now be anothe
2 CONC r daughter in this sibling circle, an NN Karlsdotter, who may have been married ed.
2 CONT
2 CONT with Magnus Minnesköld on Bjälbo in his first marriage. If so, this could really straighten out the question marks that exist why a prominent East Goth could sit as the West Goths' layman, thus the question that Åke 26. It was bec
2 CONC ause Earl Karl Eriksson's father was the Erik whom Saxo refers to as "The Earl of the Goths". For various reasons, this Gothar Earl Erik came to relocate his business to Denmark, where he was found in Zealand in the 1130s and name
2 CONC d Earl by Falster. Here again we see the close Gothic and Danish dynastic relations, when the Earl of the Goths got married to King Knut the Saint's daughter Cecilia Knutsdotter, a sister of Folke the thick wife Ingegerd Knutsdott
2 CONC er. The fact that Götajarlen Erik's son Karl Eriksson was married to a daughter of Archbishop Eskil is also evident from Saxo's information, as well as that in 1176 the spouses had at least the two sons Knut Karlsson and Karl Karl
2 CONC sson. If there was now another daughter in this sibling, who was married to Magnus Minnesköld at Bjälbo, it would be perfectly acceptable to explain how Eskil Magnusson could become Västergötland's teammate, namely that he was a d
2 CONC escendant of the Earl of Goths. Should such a genealogical theory hold, Eskil Magnusson would be a grandson's son to the Earl of the Goths, a particularly suitable kinship for a Västergötland lawman.  However, this picture is dist
2 CONC urbed by the fact that Magnus Minnesköld and one NN Karlsdotter would be relatives, as shown in Table 2, their respective grandmothers, Cecilia and Ingegerd, were sisters. A marriage between Magnus Minnesköld and NN Karlsdotter wo
2 CONC uld thus fall within the canon law's prohibition on marriage between siblings. Jarl Gallén is of the opinion that Magnus Minnesköld's first wife may very well have been a daughter of Archbishop Eskil's daughter in a different marr
2 CONC iage than with Halland's earl Karl Eriksson. He says: "It seems more likely because she came from a previous marriage and was a half-sister to the rebels supported by Birger Brosa Knut and Karl." On the other hand, there are sever
2 CONC al examples of how such canonical prohibitions were lifted by the Pope, if the marriage served "high purposes" and an appropriate "pecuniary donation" was made! Nor do you know how strict it is canon law's rules on prohibition on 
2 CONC marriage in the fourth paragraph de facto 27 Holmbäck and Elias Wessén travel (see below) was applied at the early time we are now Table 2: With the guidance of Saxo's Danish Chronicle, the notes of the Viceroy and Jarl Gallén's i
2 CONC nvestigation, this picture could show that Västergötland's teammate Eskil Magnusson, son of Magnus Minnesköld at Bjälbo in Östergötland, held the teamman's post in Västergötland on the grounds that he was a descendant. Earl of the
2 CONC  Goths Erik. The Earl of the Goths is likely to be connected with the Eriksberg royal estate in Gäsene, here in Västergötland, on which farm King Knut Eriksson, according to Vidhemsprästen, died in 1195 or 1196, after which he is 
2 CONC buried in Varnhem's monastery church. According to this arrangement, Lagman Eskil's name may be applied for in Lund, Archbishop Eskil. Furthermore, a close relationship could be demonstrated between the Erikska royal family and th
2 CONC e Folkungaätten. As stated in the text, the image of Eskil Magnusson as a descendant of the Gothic Earl Erik is disturbed by the fact that Magnus Minnesköld and an NN Karlsdotter would be siblings. Marriages between chieftains vio
2 CONC lated the rules of canon law, which could, however, be abolished by the Pope. However, it should be noted that one of Magnus Minnesköld's older sons is Bishop Karl Magnusson in Linköping, who could be named after his possible gran
2 CONC dfather Karl Eriksson.
