1 NOTE Olaf Skotkonung was the first Swedish king to become a Christian. From about AD 800, Swedish Vikings established colonies in other countries, especially Russia and Eastern Europe, and established trade routes. During the reign of 
2 CONC Eric IX, from 1150 to 1160, Swedish power was strengthened. Eric invaded Finland and forced Christianity on those he conquered; during the subsequent two centuries Finland was completely subjugated by the Swedes. Eric was allegedl
2 CONC y slain by a Danish claimant of his throne while he was attending mass, and he later became the patron saint of Sweden. [CARPENTE.GED]
