2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siemomys%C5%82 Siemomysł on Wikipedia in English]
2 CONT
2 CONT Siemomysł is the third legendary Polish duke, and said to be the father of Poland's first historical ruler, Mieszko I. Siemomysł is credited with leaving the lands known as Greater Poland to his son, who further expanded them duri
2 CONC ng his reign.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/piast/piast1.html
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Piast family=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ziemomysl, Ct of Poland (922-962), +ca 962/963 (possibly a son of Leszek)'''; He had issue:
2 CONT *A1. son, +963
2 CONT *A2. Czcibór, +after 24.6.972
2 CONT *A3. Mieszko I, baptized in 966, Ct of Poland (962-993), *922, +Poznan 25.5.992, bur St.Peter, Poznan; 1m: NN; 2m: 965 Dobrava of Bohemia (*ca 937 +977); 3m: 979/980 Oda (+1023) dau.of Gf Dietrich von Haldensleben, Mgve of the Nor
2 CONC dmark
2 CONT ** ... A4. Adleta, +after 997; 1m: Mihály Arpád (+ca 978); 2m: ca 980 Geza of Hungary (+1.2.997)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ziemomysł
2 CONT
2 CONT tytuł	- książę polski 	   urodzony	-	około 900 r.	   zmarł	-	przed 963 r.	   dynastia	-	Piastowie	   herb	-	Orzeł Piastowski	  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodzice :
2 CONT   ojciec	- 	Leszek	  
2 CONT   matka	- 	NN	  
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodzina
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 . 	żona - (kilka żon poganek)	 	od : X w. 	Potomstwo z tego związku 	     1 . 	syn 	- Mieszko I	    	     2 . 	syn 	- Prokuj	 	     3 . 	syn 	- Czcibór	 	     4 . 	córka 	- Adelajda	
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 913-963 talet
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT na jego następcę był przeznaczony syn Leszek, młodszy brat Mieszka, co najmniej o osiem lat - Mieszko w dniu postrzyżyn, w wieku siedmiu lat, miał być jedynym synem Ziemomysła i to niewidomym - Ziemomysł pod koniec swojego życia w
2 CONC yraził wolę, aby na jego następcę wybrać Mieszka.
2 CONT
2 CONT He supposedly ruled from around 930, though some historians believe that it could have been from 950. Earlier theories by Adam Naruszewicz proposed that Siemomysł's reign could have begun as early as 913.[3] However, this view is 
2 CONC not accepted by contemporary historians.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed that Siemomysł united the lands of the Western Polans, the Goplans, and the Masovians.[5] It is possible that his father, Lestek, was the first to begin this process of unification in order to establish a centralise
2 CONC d state what would later become the Duchy of Poland in 966 AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Siemomysł's wife (or wives) is also a matter of debate. There is a theory that the daughter of Włodzisław, prince of the Lendians tribe, could have been Siemomysł's wife, but there is no historical evidence to support 
2 CONC this. Formerly, it was thought that his wife was named Gorka, but Oswald Balzer refuted this view in 1895. Mieszko and Czcibor were his known sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://slovene.online/slavic-tribes/slavic-tribes-lendians/
2 CONT
2 CONT According to modern Polish historian Henryk Łowmiański, Siemomysł aided the Ukrani uprising against the Germans in 954 AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siemomysł died sometime between 950 and 960, though the latter is more probable according to 19th-century and 20th-century sources.[6] His burial place is unknown.
