1 NOTE Strachkvas (Kristián) (28 September 929 or 935, Prague - 996, Prague) was a prince of Bohemia, son of Boleslav I and brother of Boleslav II, member of the Premyslid dynasty. A clergyman, he finally became the Bishop of Prague but
2 CONC  died during consecration.
2 CONT
2 CONT Strachkvas was born during a feast where his father committed a fratricide (of Wenceslaus), which resulted in his becoming a Duke. Being remorseful of what had happened, Boleslav gave his newborn son a strange name "Strachkvas", w
2 CONC hich meant "a dreadful feast". He promised to devote his son to religion & educate him as a clergyman - he kept his word.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Cosmas' chronicle, in 994 St. Adalbert offered his episcopal see to Strachkvas, explaining that Strachkvas came from the Premyslids, and it would be easy for him to bend people to his will. Strachkvas, nevertheless, r
2 CONC ejected to accept the post. However, in 995 when Adalbert's family was massacred and he left Prague, Strachkvas was appointed to be his successor. When he was going to assume the bishop office in Prague, he suddenly died during th
2 CONC e ceremony. The circumstances of his death are still unclear.
