2 CONT http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oda_Mi%C5%9Bnie%C5%84ska
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oda_of_Meissen
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father	Eckard I, Margrave of Meissen
2 CONT *Mother	Suanhilde of Saxony
2 CONT *Born	c. 996
2 CONT *Died	After 1018
2 CONT *Spouse	Bolesław I Chrobry
2 CONT *Issue	Matilda of Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEISSEN.htm#Odadied1025
2 CONT
2 CONT vii)      '''ODA (-1025)'''.  Thietmar records the marriage of "Oda, Markgraf Ekkehard's daughter" and Boleslav in Zützen in 1018 "after septuagesima" (2 Feb)[149].  The chronicler adds the comment "until now she has lived outside
2 CONC  the law of matrimony and thus in a manner worthy only of a marriage such as this one", which suggests a reputation for moral dissolution.  m (Burg Cziczani 3 Feb 1018) as his [fourth/fifth] wife, BOŁESLAW I "Chrobry" Prince of Po
2 CONC land, son of MIESZKO I Prince of Poland & his second wife Dobrava [Dobroslawa] of Bohemia ([967]-17 Jun 1025).  He declared himself King of Poland in 1024. 
