1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The parentage of Ealdgȳð "Swann hnesce"
2 CONT (Edith the Fair) is uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marek Skarbek-Kozietulski, in More about Magnus, Count of Wroclaw, suggests that  Edith may be a daughter of Magnus “the Good” Olavsson, King of Norway.  Magnus was not a common name at that time.  Olav’s son and Edith’s son may h
2 CONC ave been the only two people in the 11th century with that name until Olav’s nephew Magnus Haraldsson was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other sources, based on the Chronicon ex Chronicis of Florence of Worcester and John of Worcester (Florentius Wigorniensis and Ioannes Wigorniensis, two 11th-12th century monks), suggest that Edith is the daughter of Thorkell the 
2 CONC Tall (Torkjell Høge Haraldsson) and Eadgyth, Lady Of Mercia (daughter of Aethelred the Unready).
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT Ealdgyth Ealdgȳð Swann hnesce "Swan neck"
2 CONT
2 CONT NOT Ealdgyth of Mercia
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress of Harold Godwinsson
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Harold and his mistress, probably Eadgyth Swanneshals:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Godwin
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Edmund
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Magnus
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Gytha
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. (Ulf?)
2 CONT
