2 CONC vered Abbot of Rievaulx, to whom is generally attributed the vita in Latin, a hagiography partly based on materials in an earlier vita by Osbert de Clare and which in its turn provided the material for a rhymed version in octasyll
2 CONC abic Anglo-Norman, possibly written by the chronicler Matthew Paris. At the time of Edward's canonisation, saints were broadly categorised as either martyrs or confessors. Martyrs were people who had been killed for their faith, w
2 CONC hile confessors were saints who had died natural deaths. Edward was accordingly styled Edward the Confessor, partly to distinguish him from his canonised predecessor Edward the Martyr.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Roman Catholic Church regards St Edward the Confessor as the patron saint of kings, difficult marriages, and separated spouses. After the reign of Henry II, Edward was considered to be the "Patron Saint of England", until 1348
2 CONC  when he was replaced in this role by Saint George. St Edward remains the "Patron Saint of the Royal Family".
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward's reign is memorialized in an eight panel stained glass window within St Laurence Church, Ludlow, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT The shrine of Saint Edward the Confessor remains where it was after the final relocation of his body in the 13th century - at the heart of Westminster Abbey, where the date of his translation, 13 October, is observed as a major fe
2 CONC ast. For some time the Abbey had claimed that it possessed a set of coronation regalia that Edward had left for use in all future coronations. Following Edward's canonization, these were regarded as holy relics, and thereafter the
2 CONC y were used at all English coronations from the 13th Century until the destruction of the regalia by Oliver Cromwell in 1649.
2 CONT
2 CONT The main liturgical commemoration of Saint Edward is on the date of his translation, 13 October, rather than the date of his death. This feast was removed from the General Roman Calendar when it was reformed in 1969, but remains i
2 CONC n the Calendar of the Traditional Latin Mass, as well as the national calendar of the Roman Catholic Church in England. The Church of England has included this feast in its calendar since the Book of Common Prayer of 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT In popular culture
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward is depicted as the central saint of the Wilton Diptych, a devotional piece made for Richard II, but now in the collection of the National Gallery. The reverse of the piece carries Edward's arms; and Richard's badge of a whi
2 CONC te hart. The panel painting dates from the end of the 14th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward the Confessor is referred to by characters in Shakespeare's play The Tragedy of Macbeth as the saintly king of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the central figure in Alfred Duggan's 1960 historical novel The Cunning of the Dove.
2 CONT
2 CONT On screen he has been portrayed by Eduard Franz in the film Lady Godiva of Coventry (1955), George Howe in the BBC TV drama series Hereward the Wake (1965), Donald Eccles in the two-part BBC TV play Conquest (1966; part of the ser
2 CONC ies Theatre 625), Brian Blessed in Macbeth (1997), based on the Shakespeare play (although he does not appear in the play itself), and Adam Woodroffe in an episode of the British TV series Historyonics entitled "1066" (2004). In 2
2 CONC 002, he was portrayed by Lennox Greaves in the Doctor Who audio adventure Seasons of Fear.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT SAN EDUARDO EL CONFESOR, REY DE INGLATERRA
2 CONT
2 CONT Venid, benditos de mi Padre, a tomar posesión del reino que os está preparado desde la creación del mundo. (Mateo, 25, 34).
2 CONT
2 CONT Eduardo III, sabio y profundo legislador, pasó primero 35 años en Normandía durante el reinado de los invasores normandos. Llamado a Inglaterra por el concierto unánime de las voluntades, hizo florecer en ella la justicia y la paz
2 CONC . Edificó numerosas iglesias y fundó la abadía de Westminster. Extremadamente caritativo, llevó un día a un pobre en sus espaldas y le dio una sortija de gran valor. Nada rehusaba de lo que se le pedía en nombre de San Juan Evange
2 CONC lista, el cual le advirtió sobre la hora de su muerte, acaecida en 1066 a la edad de 65 años.
2 CONT
2 CONT MEDITACIÓN SOBRE LA FELICIDAD DEL HOMBRE EN ESTA VIDA
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Tres cosas pueden hacernos felices, tanto al menos cuanto lo podemos ser en este lugar de destierro. La primera es la buena conciencia: sin ella, ni los placeres, ni los honores, ni el cumplimiento de todos nuestros deseos podr
2 CONC ían contentarnos. Si tienes el alma pura, todo lo desagradable que pueda sucederte no debe turbarte. ¡Qué consuelo poder decirse: Hago lo que depende de mi para estar bien con Dios! ¿Puedes, tú, con verdad, decirlo? ¿No te reproch
2 CONC a nada tu conciencia?
2 CONT
2 CONT II. La segunda condición para ser feliz es abandonarse generosamente a la providencia de Dios, consagrarse a Él sin reserva, no querer sino lo que El quiere y recibir de su mano con agradecimiento el bien y el mal, pues lo uno y l
2 CONC o otro son efectos de su bondad. Las aflicciones, el ayuno, las enfermedades, no son penosos para los que los soportan, sino solamente para los que los reciben a disgusto. (Salmo).
2 CONT
2 CONT III. La tercera condición es considerar cuál es voluntad de Dios en todo lo que nos acaece. Dios tiene sus designios y el demonio los suyos. ¿Cuál es designio de Dios en esta enfermedad que te envía? Que la soportes con resignació
2 CONC n, mediante el pensamiento de la muerte y del paraíso. El demonio, por lado, quiere arrojarte en la impaciencia y en la murmuración. Dios es tan bueno que no permitiría más que sucediese ningún mal en el mundo, si no fuese lo sufi
2 CONC cientemente poderoso como para sacar bien del mal. (San Agustín). Conformidad con la voluntad de Dios Orad por los que os gobiernan.
2 CONT
2 CONT ORACIÓN
2 CONT
2 CONT Oh Dios, que habéis coronado con la gloria eterna al bienaventurado rey Eduardo, vuestro confesor, haced, os Lo suplicamos, que honrándolo en la tierra, podamos reinar un día con él en el cielo. Por J. C. N. S. Amén.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hay estampa, Texto tomado de: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  http://caballerodelainmaculada.blogspot.com/2009/10/san-eduardo-el-confesor-rey-de.html
2 CONT
