1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jens Kjærulf was married to Anne Nielsdatter Griis of the noble family from Slette and probably the daughter of Niels Griis (married to Bodil Svendsdatter Orning), who in 1505 together with her father Palle Griis l
2 CONC ived in Ø. Mellerup in the parish of Jerslev , and who in 1545 was accused of capital offence (Halsløsning) after the Count's War (Klementsfejden) ; Dyrskjøt says: "Fru Anne Griis of Slette, Niels Grise's daughter, Baggi Kierulff'
2 CONC s sister" , but he has apparently by mistake written Kierulff instead of Griis, and Niels Griis had in fact a son called Bagge, supposedly named after Niels Griis' brother Bagge, who lived in the neighbourhood of Kornumgaard, name
2 CONC ly on Hjermeslevgaard, and became known for his attempt to kill Skipper Clement - an attempt - for which he had to pay with his own life.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Nielsdatter Griis, død før 1606, gift med herredsfoged Jens Andersen Kjærulf i Kornumgård, V.Brønderslev sogn, død 1606. Der blev afholdt skifte efter Jens Andersen Kjærulf og hustru Anne Griis den 18.11.1606. Ægteparret, der
2 CONC  antagelig er begravet i Brønderslev kirke, gav 1596 de svære alterstager, der endnu findes i kirken, og som bærer begges våbenskjolde med henholdsvis en ulv og en vildbasse. Kirkens øverste stolestader skal ligeledes forhen have 
2 CONC båret deres våbener.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Griis var af den adelige slægt Griis af Slette i Han Herred. Hendes broder Bagge Griis på Hjermeslevgaard blev bekendt for sit drabsforsøg på skipper Klement i 1534.
