1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Genealogical Note:'''
2 CONT This profile represents a '''reconstructed genealogical link'''. No primary documents directly recording this individual's name have survived. However, his existence is postulated by researchers based on:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1. Naming traditions:''' His son Laurits (fl. 1519) named his firstborn Hans/Jens, which, according to the customs of the time, strongly points to the grandfather's name.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2. Chronology:''' He serves as the necessary generational link between Laurits Jonsen (fl. 1484) and Laurits of True (fl. 1519).
2 CONT According to NST research, this is the most probable family structure explaining the ancestry of Rev. Jens Larsen Bugge (1542-1612).
