2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hjerm Ladle Farm or Hjermitslevgård  is a manor house in Tolstrup parish in Vendsyssel. the manor house has a stone house which is the oldest dwelling house in North Jutland (year of construction is uncertain but mL. 1540 and 1570
2 CONC ). Half-timbered wing from around 1650 is one of the few "farmhand wings" that exists in Denmark . the manor is a tower foundation from the Middle Ages. The newer building is from 1883. Hjermitslevgaard included in the Eastern Hje
2 CONC rmitslev, a unique ribbon building. The barn is built of the original barn from 1793 is one of the longest running behind.  Vognsen  in the 13th century. Owned adelslægten Vognsen farm. It was a rich family, with many estates in V
2 CONC endsyssel, among andre Fuglsig at Hjørring. The last Vognsen on the farm was Morten Johansen Vognsen who drowned in 1498 in conjunction with her father. MJ had three daughters of whom one of them married a noble family and was giv
2 CONC en the right to inherit the farm. It was Mette Vognsen and she married in Bagge Pallesen Griis. Griis died in 1534 in an attempt to turn Skipper Clement death. Mette Vognsen then married Jens Thomesen Dan.  About 1400 owners Niels
2 CONC  Vognsen about 1425 Inger Hermansdatter Pennow about 1444 Morten Nielsen 1471 Niels Mortensen 1481 Johan Mortensen Morten Johansen in 1542 about Dorte Jespersdatter Lunow about 1550 Svend Orning and Jens Thomesen Dan 
2 CONT
