2 CONT 3) Anne, † 1540, GM Niels Kaas (with a Sparre of the weapon) to the Thaarup Overgaard, † 1035.  c) Yep Andersen Muus to Randrup (Hellum H), founded in 1492 soul fairs, was 1493 Hofsinde, founded in 1509 Messer in Holy house in Ran
2 CONC ders, certainly † unmarried.  d) Erik Andersen probably † small.  e) Niels Andersen probably † small.  f) Margaret, 1495 lived on Støvringgaard, GM Axel Jepsen, (Thott) to Støvringgaard, was † 1490; on Værgemaalet and legacy of th
2 CONC eir minds weak daughter were brought great strife between the Bjørn'er and Axel's kinsmen.  g) Sophie, GM Herman Fleming to Bavelse (he g. 2. m. Anne Eriksdatter Thott).  h) Inger to Randrup, g. 1. m. Niels Jensen (Munk with the v
2 CONC ine of the weapon) to the Visborg that led main banner in Slagct by Brunkebjerg but died shortly after 2 m. Jens Tygesen (Seefeld) to Dalsgaard.  i) Anne, GM Eight Emmiksen to Refsø. 
