2 CONT PŘEMYSL OTAKAR of Bohemia, son of WENZEL I King of Bohemia & his wife Kunigunde von Hohenstaufen (1233-killed in battle Dürnkrut 26 Aug 1278, bur Znaim Minoriten). The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "Wladislaum et 
2 CONC Przesemysl" as the two sons of "Rex Wencezslaus"[301]. Associate king of Bohemia 31 Jul 1248-Nov 1249. Markgraf of Moravia 1251. He succeeded as OTAKAR Duke of Austria and Steiermark in 1251. He succeeded his father in 1253 as OTA
2 CONC KAR PŘEMYSL II King of Bohemia. Crowned 1261. His possession of the duchies of Austria and Styria was legalised in 1262 by Richard of Cornwall King of Germany[302]. "Otakarus…rex Boemiæ, dux Austriæ et Stiriæ et marchio Moraviæ" f
2 CONC ounded Kloster Goldenkron by charter dated 1263[303]. "Otacharus…rex Boemorum dux Austrie et Styrie et marchio Moravie" confirmed the foundation of Kloster Hohenfurt by "Wockonis quondam marschalci regni nostri" by charter dated 1
2 CONC 7 Jul 1264[304]. King Richard appointed Otakar as protector of the royal domains east of the Rhine 7 Jan 1267[305]. He succeeded in 1269 as OTAKAR Duke of Carinthia, . In 1274, King Otakar ignored demands for the return to imperia
2 CONC l jurisdiction of the duchies of Austria, Carinthia and Styria. This proposal had been made in line with the policy of Rudolf I King of Germany, promulgated at the Diet of Nürnburg 19 Nov 1274, under which all properties unlawfull
2 CONC y appropriated since the deposition of Emperor Friedrich II in 1245 were to be returned to the empire. In accordance with the procedures established, the duchies were deemed forfeited after a year and a day[306]. King Rudolf decla
2 CONC red war on Bohemia, and King Otakar was obliged to abdicate under the temporary peace of 21 Nov 1276, which was confirmed by treaty 6 May 1277. Rudolf's position was confirmed definitively after he defeated King Otakar at the batt
2 CONC le of Marchfeld near Dürnkrut 26 Aug 1278. The Notæ Altahenses record that "Otakarus rex Boemie" was killed in battle "1278 VII Kal Sep"[307].
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly (Hainburg 11 Feb 1252, dispensation 3o and 4o 5 Jul 1253, repudiated 1261) as her second husband, MARGARETA of Austria, widow of HEINRICH VII King of Germany, daughter of LEOPOLD VI Duke of Austria [Babenberg] & his wife
2 CONC  Theodora --- (-Burg Krumau am Kamp 2 Oct 1267, bur Lilienfeld). The Annales Mellicenses in 1226 record the marriage of "Margaretam filiam Liupoldi ducis Austrie" and "Heinricus filius imperatoris Friderici"[308]. The Notæ Sancti 
2 CONC Emeranni record the marriage in 1225 at Nürnberg of "Heinricus rex" and "Constantiam filiam Liupoldi ducis Austrie"[309]. She was crowned Queen of Germany 28 Mar 1227 at Aachen. She lived in a Dominican convent at Trier after the 
2 CONC death of her first husband[310]. The Continuatio Garstensis records the second marriage "apud Heimburch" of "Margaretam viduam regis Heinrici, filiam ducis Leupoldi" and "Otakarus marchio Moravie"[311]. The Canonicorum Pragensium 
2 CONC Continuationes Cosmæ records the marriage "in Henburk III Id Feb 1252" of "Prziemysl filius regis Wenceslai" and "Margaretham viduam filiam Leupoldi ducis Austriæ"[312]. The Chronicon Francisci records the marriage in 1252 of "Ott
2 CONC akarus Rex Boemiæ" and "Margaretham, quondam Romanorum Regina"[313]. "Margareta domina regni Boemie ducissa Austrie et Styrie marchionissa Moravie" granted "comitiam in Rakz" to "Wocconi de Rosenberch" by charter dated 1260[314]. 
2 CONC The Altahenses Annales record that "Otaker rex" repudiated his first wife "sine iudicio ecclesie"[315]. The Canonicorum Pragensium Continuationes Cosmæ records that "regina Margareta" left Bohemia for Austria "XV Kal Nov 1261"[316
2 CONC ]. The necrology of Lilienfeld records the death "IV Kal Nov" of "Margareta quondam regina Romanorum filia ducis Leupoldi" and her burial next to her father "in Campo Liliorum"[317]. The necrology of Kloster Neuburg records the de
2 CONC ath "IV Kal Nov" of "Margareta filia ducis Liupoldi regina Romanorum ducissa Austrie et Stirie"[318].
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (Pressburg 25 Oct 1261) as her first husband, KUNIGUNDA [Kunguta] Rostislavna, daughter of ROSTISLAV Mikhailovich ex-Grand Prince of Kiev, ex-Prince of Galich, Ban of Mačva & his wife Anna of Hungary (1245-9 Sep 1285, b
2 CONC ur Prague Erlöserkirche). The Canonicorum Pragensium Continuationes Cosmæ records the marriage "VIII Kal Nov 1261" of "Cunegundem filiam Hostislai ducis Bulgarorum" and the king "in castello Ungarias…Possen"[319]. The Chronica Pra
2 CONC gensis (Chronicon Francisci) records the second marriage of "Rex Przsemysl" and "Chungundam, Regis de Mazouia filiam"[320]. The Altahenses Annales record the marriage in 1261 of "Otaker rex" and "Chunigundem filiam Regis Ruscie, n
2 CONC eptem Bele regis Ungarie ex filia"[321]. She married secondly (Prague 2 Jun 1284) as his second wife, Zaviš von Rosenberg zu Skalitz und Falkenstein (-beheaded Schloß Frauenberg 24 Aug 1290, bur Hohenfurt). The Chronica Pragensis 
2 CONC (Chronicon Francisci) records the second marriage of "rex Wencezslaus…mater…eius" and "quondam Baronem…Zauissium" by whom she had a son "in Moravia…Iohannes" who joined "ordine Cruciferorum Christo"[322]. The Cronica Aulæ Regine r
2 CONC ecords the capture and death of “Zawissium...castrum...Vroburg”[323].
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (1): --- Palczierzik, daughter of ---. The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "filium…Nicolaum, et postea filias plures" as the children of "Rex Przsemysl" and his mistress named "Palczierzik"[324]. Pulkawa’s 
2 CONC Bohemian Chronicle records (in 1252) “filiam de Kunring de Austria” as mistress of “Przemysl filius regis Wenceslai” and mother of “filium...Nicolauum...postea...ducem Opaviensem” and of “postea tres filias” who married “unam...do
2 CONC mino de Strakonicz, secundam de Wartemberg et de Druholz, tertiam...Vockoni de Krawau”[325]. Friess suggests that Pulkawa’s identification of Otakar’s mistress results from confusion with another source stating that the king’s dau
2 CONC ghter married “Heinrich V von Kuenring-Weitra” (see below)[326].
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (2): ---. The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Otakar Přemysl II & his second wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. HEINRICH (1262-1263). The Cronica Aulæ Regine records that “rex Ottacarus” and his second wife had “tres filios”, of whom “duobus mox in infantia defunctis”, while “iunior” succeeded their father[327]. The primary source which 
2 CONC confirms his name has not yet been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. son (-young). The Cronica Aulæ Regine records that “rex Ottacarus” and his second wife had “tres filios”, of whom “duobus mox in infantia defunctis”, while “iunior” succeeded their father[328].
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. KUNIGUNDE (Jan 1265-27 Nov 1321, bur Prague St Veit). The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) records the baptism of "Rex Przsemysl…filiæ suæ primogenitæ" in 1265[329]. The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) records 
2 CONC that "filia Regis…Chungundis" became a nun "ad sanctum Franciscum" in 1276, but that she was later taken from the monastery by her brother and married to "Duci Mazouiæ", after whose death she became "Abbatissa ad sanctum Georgium 
2 CONC in castro Pragensis"[330]. The primary source which confirms her first betrothal has not yet been identified. The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) records the death in 1321 of "Regis Przemysl filia, Abbatissa ad sanctum Ge
2 CONC orgium in castro Pragensi…Chunegundis" and her burial in the monastery[331]. Betrothed ([1276]%29 to HARTMANN von Habsburg Graf von Kiburg, son of RUDOLF I Graf von Habsburg King of Germany & his first wife Gertrud [Anna] von Hohe
2 CONC nberg [Zollern] (Rheinfelden 1263-drowned between Breisach and Strasbourg 21 Dec 1281, bur Basel Münster). m (1291, divorced before 19 Dec 1302) as his second wife, BOLESŁAW II Prince of Plock, son of SIEMOWIT I Prince of Mazovia 
2 CONC [Piast] & his wife Pereiaslava Daniilovich of Galich (after 1251-20 Apr 1313). He succeeded his brother in 1294 as BOLESŁAW II Prince of Mazovia.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. AGNES (5 Sep 1269-Prague 17 May 1296, bur Prague, Clarissan convent). The Canonicorum Pragensium Continuationes Cosmæ records the birth "Non Sep 1269" of "regi Otakaro filia", but does not name her[332]. The Chronica Pragensis 
2 CONC (Chronicon Francisci) records the betrothal in 1278 of "Wencezslaus filius regis Boemiæ" and "filiam Domini Rudolphi Electi" and of "filius Electi filiam Regis Boemiæ"[333]. The Dytheri de Helmestat Notæ Historicæ record that "rex
2 CONC  Rudolfus…filium suum dominum Hartmudum [error for Rudolfum]" married "sororem regis Bohemie"[334]. After her husband died, she lived at Schloß Brugg im Aargau until 1295, thereafter becoming a nun at the Clarissan convent of Prag
2 CONC ue. The Chronicon Francisci records the death "XVI Kal Jun" in 1296 of "Domina Agnes soror Regis Boemiæ, Ducissa Austriæ, relicta Ducis Rudolphi Romanorum Regis filii" and her burial "in Ecclesia sanctæ Claræ ordinis fratrum minor
2 CONC em apud sanctum Franciscum in Praga"[335]. m (contract Iglau 1278, Mar 1289) RUDOLF II von Habsburg ex-Duke of Austria, son of RUDOLF I Graf von Habsburg King of Germany & his first wife Gertrud [Anna] von Hohenberg (1270-Prague 1
2 CONC 0 May 1290, bur Prague Burg, transferred 1293 to St Veit’s Cathedral).
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. WENZEL (17 Sep 1271-21 Jun 1305, bur Prague Königsaal). The Chronicon Francisci records the birth "in die beatorum Martyrum Cozmæ et Damiani" in 1271 of "Wencezslaus…Rex Boemiæ"[336]. He succeeded in 1283 as WENZEL II King of B
2 CONC ohemia. Imperial Elector 1289. Crowned King of Bohemia 2 Jun 1297. King of Poland 1300.
2 CONT
2 CONT - see below.
2 CONT
2 CONT King Otakar Přemysl II had [seven] illegitimate children by Mistress (1):
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. NIKOLAUS ([1255]-25 Jul 1318). The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "filium…Nicolaum, et postea filias plures" as the children of "Rex Przsemysl" and his mistress named "Palczierzik", adding that he was later inve
2 CONC sted as "Dux Opauiæ"[337]. Pulkawa’s Bohemian Chronicle records (in 1252) “filiam de Kunring de Austria” as mistress of “Przemysl filius regis Wenceslai” and mother of “filium...Nicolauum...postea...ducem Opaviensem” and of “poste
2 CONC a tres filias” who married “unam...domino de Strakonicz, secundam de Wartemberg et de Druholz, tertiam...Vockoni de Krawau”[338]. He was legitimated 6 Oct 1360, but excluded from succession to the throne of Bohemia 20 Oct 1260. He
2 CONC rr von Troppau 4 Jul 1269. Ritter 1273. He was installed in 1281 as NIKOLAUS I Duke of Troppau.
2 CONT
2 CONT - DUKES of TROPPAU.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. [AGNES] . The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "filium…Nicolaum, et postea filias plures" as the children of "Rex Przsemysl" and his mistress named "Palczierzik"[339]. Pulkawa’s Bohemian Chronicle records (in 1252
2 CONC ) “filiam de Kunring de Austria” as mistress of “Przemysl filius regis Wenceslai” and mother of “filium...Nicolauum...postea...ducem Opaviensem” and of “postea tres filias” who married “unam...domino de Strakonicz, secundam de War
2 CONC temberg et de Druholz, tertiam...Vockoni de Krawau”[340]. m [BAVOR] [III] Herr von Strakonicz, son of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. daughter. The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "filium…Nicolaum, et postea filias plures" as the children of "Rex Przsemysl" and his mistress named "Palczierzik"[341]. Pulkawa’s Bohemian Chronicle records (in 1252
2 CONC ) “filiam de Kunring de Austria” as mistress of “Przemysl filius regis Wenceslai” and mother of “filium...Nicolauum...postea...ducem Opaviensem” and of “postea tres filias” who married “unam...domino de Strakonicz, secundam de War
2 CONC temberg et de Druholz, tertiam...Vockoni de Krawau”[342]. m --- Herr von Wartenberg, son of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. daughter. The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "filium…Nicolaum, et postea filias plures" as the children of "Rex Przsemysl" and his mistress named "Palczierzik"[343]. Pulkawa’s Bohemian Chronicle records (in 1252
2 CONC ) “filiam de Kunring de Austria” as mistress of “Przemysl filius regis Wenceslai” and mother of “filium...Nicolauum...postea...ducem Opaviensem” and of “postea tres filias” who married “unam...domino de Strakonicz, secundam de War
2 CONC temberg et de Druholz, tertiam...Vockoni de Krawau”[344]. m ([1276]%29 WOK Herr von Krawarz, son of --- (-[1329]).
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. [JESEK ([1265/70]-26 Aug 1296, bur Wysehrad). The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified. Priest at Wysehrad 1290.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. GISELA [Elisabeth?] . The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "filium…Nicolaum, et postea filias plures" as the children of "Rex Przsemysl" and his mistress named "Palczierzik"[345]. The Cronica Aulæ Regine names “d
2 CONC omina Gisela coniuge domini Wikardi de Polna...regis Ottacari filia”[346]. Friess records Balbin noting the marriage of Otakar’s daughter Elisabeth and “Wikard de Polna, einem böhmischen Magnaten”, suggesting that she was the same
2 CONC  person as the other Elisabeth shown below, Vikard being her second husband[347]. Balbin in fact records “Gisela Wikardi de Polna uxor”, without any indication of the source on which this information is based[348]. m VIKARD Herr v
2 CONC on Polna Burggraf of Brno, son of --- (-after 1303).
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. [daughter. The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified. m (after May 1277) --- Herr von Weitra, son of ---.]
2 CONT
2 CONT King Otakar Přemysl II had one illegitimate child by [Mistress (2)]:
2 CONT
2 CONT 13. ELISABETH . A letter of King Otakar II dated Mar 1277 records that “H[enricus] de Witra...filius suus” had married “nostram...filiam”[349]. “Heinrich von Kuenring, Marschall und Capitaneus von Oesterrecih...seiner Gattin Elisa
2 CONC bet” settled differences with the provost of Klosterneuburg by charter dated 25 Mar 1276[350]. “Henricus senior de Witra, Chunigundis uxor nostra, Henricus et Albero filii nostri et Elisabet nurus mea Henrici filii nostri legitima
2 CONC ” granted property to Otto von Dünstein by charter dated 29 Jan 1278[351]. m (before 25 Mar 1276) HEINRICH [V] von Kuenring-Weitra, son of HEINRICH [IV] von Kuenring-Weitra & his wife Kunigunde --- (-Troppau Jul 1281). Marshall of
2 CONC  Austria. https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BOHEMIA.htm
