2 CONT 11.       GISELA [Elisabeth?] .  The Chronica Pragensis (Chronicon Francisci) names "filium…Nicolaum, et postea filias plures" as the children of "Rex Przsemysl" and his mistress named "Palczierzik"[345].  The Cronica Aulæ Regine 
2 CONC names “domina Gisela coniuge domini Wikardi de Polna...regis Ottacari filia”[346].  Friess records Balbin noting the marriage of Otakar’s daughter Elisabeth and “Wikard de Polna, einem böhmischen Magnaten”, suggesting that she was
2 CONC  the same person as the other Elisabeth shown below, Vikard being her second husband[347].  Balbin in fact records “Gisela Wikardi de Polna uxor”, without any indication of the source on which this information is based[348].  m VI
2 CONC KARD Herr von Polna Burggraf of Brno, son of --- (-after 1303).  
