2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Albrecht II of Brandenburg'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Albrecht II (* around/after 1150; † 25 February 1220) was the Margrave of Brandenburg from 1205 until his death. The Ascanians Albrecht II was the youngest son of Otto I and the Polish Duke's daughter Judith of Poland as well as t
2 CONC he grandson of Albrecht the Bear, the founder of the Mark Brandenburg in the year 1157. He took over the Mark County after the death of his eldest brother Otto II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Monument in the former Victory Avenue, Berlin 1898
2 CONT
2 CONT When he died, his two sons were still unwilling. The feudal guardianship first took over Archbishop Albrecht of Magdeburg, from 1221 the mother, Countess Mathilde. Since their death in the year 1225, the brothers have led the coun
2 CONC ty together.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Albrecht was married since 1205 with Mathilde von Groitzsch (1185 – 1225), daughter of Count Konrad II (Lusatia) from the sex of the contest, and the Polish Duke's daughter Elisabeth from the sex of the piasts. With her he had fou
2 CONC r children:
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Johann I. (* ca. 1213; † 4. April 1266)
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Otto III. der Fromme (* 1215; † 9. Oktober 1267)
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Mechthild (* ?; † 10. Juni 1261), ∞ 1228 Welfenherzog Otto I. von Lüneburg (* 1204; † 1252), auch Otto das Kind genannt
2 CONT
2 CONT -4. Elisabeth (* 1207; † 19. November 1231)[2], ∞ 1228 Landgraf Heinrich Raspe von Thüringen (* 1201; † 1247)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albrecht II. Brandenburg  Wikipedia Albrecht II]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia: Albrecht II of Brandenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT -Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Albrecht II (* around/after 1150; † 25 February 1220) was the Margrave of Brandenburg from 1205 until his death. The Ascanians Albrecht II was the youngest son of Otto I and the Polish Duke's daughter Judith of Poland as well as t
2 CONC he grandson of Albrecht the Bear, the founder of the Mark Brandenburg in the year 1157. He took over the Mark County after the death of his eldest brother Otto II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Monument in the former Victory Avenue, Berlin 1898
2 CONT
2 CONT * Johann I. (ca. 1213 - 4. April 1266)
2 CONT
2 CONT  * Otto III. der Fromme (1215 - 9. October 1267)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mechthild (? - 10. Juni 1261) ∞ 1228 Welf Herzog Otto I of Lüneburg (1204-1252), also called Otto the Child
2 CONT
2 CONT * Elisabeth (ca 1206 - ca. 1231) ∞ 1228 Landgrave Heinrich Raspe of Thuringia (1201-1247)
2 CONT
2 CONT At his death, the two sons were still immature. The feudal guardianship first took over Archbishop Albrecht of Magdeburg, from 1221 the mother, Countess Mathilde. Since their death in the year 1225, the brothers have led the count
2 CONC y together
2 CONT
2 CONT Monument of Albrecht II in the Berlin Victory Avenue 
2 CONT
2 CONT The aforementioned monument of Albrecht stood in the former Victory Avenue in the Tiergarten in Berlin, the 1895 by Kaiser Wilhelm II commissioned "Splendor Boulevard" with monuments from the history of Brandenburg and Prussia. Un
2 CONC der the direction of Reinhold Begas, between 1895 and 1901 27 sculptor 32 still images of the Brandenburg and Prussian rulers of 2.75 m height were created. Each statue was flanked by two smaller busts with the portrayal of person
2 CONC s who had played an important role in the life of the respective ruler or for the history of Brandenburg/Prussia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beside Figure Eike von Repgow, writer of the Saxon Mirror
2 CONT
2 CONT At the Monument Group 4 were the busts of Eike von Repgow, the author of the Saxon Mirror, and Hermann von Salza, the high master of the Teutonic Order. As Albrecht's participation in his founding meeting shows (see above), he had
2 CONC  gained a close relationship with the German Knights, which was based on the same political objective with regard to the eastern territories. He had already met Hermann von Salza on the Palestine Crusade and deepened his relations
2 CONC hip with life – the choice of a minor character is meant to express this relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Eike von Repgow, neither Albrecht II nor the Mark Brandenburg were in contact with Gustav Albrecht. The choice of the secondary figure is probably due to the fact that the Saxon mirror as the most important legal book
2 CONC  of the German Middle Ages had great influence also on Brandenburg and northern Germany. However, Eike had a close connection to the House of Ascanians, for he was in the service of Heinrich I, Prince of Anhalt.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sculptor of the monument Group was Johannes Böse. The revelation took place on March 22nd, 1898. The monument of Albrecht, Gustav Albrecht 1900, described as follows: "The Margrave, in the chain tank with a high-pitched hood, 
2 CONC is conceived in a battle-ready position, as he protected with dragged heavy a castle, presumably the border-resistant Oderberg built in the year 1215. The head of the energetically looking prince adorns a narrow Kronreif; Around t
2 CONC he armored shirt adorned with the Märkische Eagle is a broad ornamental belt, a long coat falls, held together by the left, picturesquely back down. " 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT  1. ↑ Stephan Warnatsch, S. 26
2 CONT
2 CONT  2. ↑ Gustav Albrecht, S. 88f
2 CONT
