1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=johanson&id=I65898
2 CONT
2 CONT * •ID: I65898 
2 CONT * •Name: Mathilde von LANDSBERG 1 
2 CONT * •Sex: F 
2 CONT * •Birth: ABT 1185 in Landsberg, Bavaria, Germany 
2 CONT * •Death: 1255
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p781.htm#i7805
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Konrad von LANDSBERG b: ABT 1158 in Landsberg, Bavaria, Germany  Mother: ELZBIETA of Poland b: 1152 in Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 ALBRECHT von BRANDENBURG b: ABT 1180 in Brandenburg, Germany Children 1. Otto von BRANDENBURG IV b: ABT 1209 in Brandenburg, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 1.Author: Charles Cawley Title: Medieval Lands Publication: Name: Copyright FMG and Charles Cawley 2006; Location: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/Contents.htm; Repository:  Name: Internet
2 CONT
2 CONT Text: MATHILDE (-Salzwedel 1255, bur Kloster Lehnin). The Chronicon Montis Serreni records the marriage in 1205 of "Machtildem" older of the two daughters of "Conradi marchionis Orientalis" and "Albertus Brandenburgensis marchio"[
2 CONC 218]. The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Machtildem…et Agnetem" as the two daughters of "Conradus marchio filius Dedonis" & his wife, specifying that Mathilde married "Albertus…marchio de Brandenburc"[219]. The Cronica Principum S
2 CONC axonie names "Mechtildem filiam Conradi marchionis de Landesberch" as wife of "Albertus secundus"[220]. The Cronica Principum Saxonie records the death in 1255 of "Mechtildis [uxor Alberti secundi]" and her burial at Lehnin[221]. 
2 CONC m (Aug 1205) ALBRECHT II Markgraf von Brandenburg, son of OTTO I Markgraf von Brandenburg [Askanier] & his second wife Ada of Holland (Jan after [1172/75]-25 Feb 1220, bur Kloster Lehnin). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathilde_von_Brandenburg http://olypen.com/zob/genealogy/Europe-tree/Wettin/Wettin.html
