1 CONC on. Etter Olav Trygvessons fall fulgte hun antagelig sin mann til Norge, men vi hører ikke mer om hennes videre skjebne.
0 @N6000000002187734479@ NOTE Harald II of Denmark
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Harald II of Denmark (c. 994–1018) was king of Denmark from 1014 to 1018. He was the eldest son of Sweyn I of Denmark and Gunhilda and was regent while his father was fighting Ethelred the Unready in England. He inherited the Dani
1 CONC sh throne in 1014 and died in 1018. After his death, he was succeeded by his brother, Canute.
1 CONT
1 CONT Harald II
1 CONT Born: c. 994 Died: 1018 
1 CONT Regnal titles 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Sweyn Forkbeard King of Denmark
1 CONT 1014-1018 Succeeded by
1 CONT Canute the Great 
0 @N6000000000437164045@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> King Name Suffix:<NSFX> I, of Denmark, England and Norway "The Great" Danish king of England (1016–35), Denmark (1019–35), and Norway (1028–35). Danish Knut He helped his father, Sweyn I , invade England in 1013
1 CONC . Sweyn was accepted as king of England after exiling King Ethelred II  but died in1014; Canute returned and defeated Ethelred's son to win the English throne in1016. At first he ruled ruthlessly, killing English opponents and app
1 CONC ointing Danes in their places, but within a few years he had married Ethelred's widow and was granting earldoms to Englishmen. Canute proved an effective ruler who brought peace and prosperity to England, issued an important law c
1 CONC ode, and becamea strong supporter of the church. With English help he secured the throne of Denmark on his brother's death. His early death and that of his sons led to the restoration of Ethelred's dynasty
