0 @N6000000002187734508@ NOTE Torkel Styrbjörnsson
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Torkel Styrbjörnsson, Torgils, Sprakalägg or Sprakling is considered to have been the son of the disinherited Swedish prince Styrbjörn the Strong, the son of king Olof (II) Björnsson of Sweden. His mother was Tyra, the daughter of
1 CONC  Harold Bluetooth (king of Denmark and Norway).
1 CONT
1 CONT He died at the Battle of Swold.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Ulf Jarl (d. 1027), the Jarl of Canute the Great in Denmark and Danish steward. 
1 CONT Gytha Thorkelsdóttir who was to marry Godwin, Earl of Wessex. 
