1 CONT
1 CONT SOURCES:
1 CONT 1.  Stuart, Roderick W.  _Royalty for Commoners_.  2nd Edition. Baltimore,
1 CONT MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1992; line 166-33.  He was the
1 CONT Forester of Arques.
1 CONT
1 CONT Harald refused to accept the crown until he had first performed his father's obsequies with all the magnificence becoming his highrank. One of his earliest was the conquest of Norway, which became a province of Denmark. Styrbear, 
1 CONC King of Sweden, solicited the aid of King Harold in one of his wars, and to enforce his request he brought along with him Gyntha, his sister, a lady of admirable beauty. The stratagem had the intended effect; HaroldBluetooth becam
1 CONC e enamored and married her. The progress of Christianity gainedsome headway during his reign, and the King received baptism, and erected a splendid church. His daughter Gunilda married Richard I, Duke of Normandy.
0 @N6000000002187576590@ NOTE Harald I "Blaatand" Gornsson King of Denmark
1 CONT
1 CONT Born: Abt 910
1 CONT
1 CONT Married to Gyrithe Olafsdotter Queen of Denmark
1 CONT
1 CONT Died: 1 Nov 987
