0 @N6000000001744891841@ NOTE [s2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Source: Church of JC of the LDS "Ancestral File" CD-Rom database, ver 4.17. Dates of last 3 children's births indicate that they may have had a younger mother than the oldest two.
1 CONT
1 CONT From Gayle Wilson <gayle@inforum.net>: R. Allen Brown is of the opinion that Gunnor's father was a 'Danico', a Dane who was welcomed and permitted to settle in Normandy. Later , as more Danes appeared, this man joined their rebell
1 CONC ions and became a fierce war-leader who was giving Duke Richard trouble. Brown says that Richard married Gunnor 'in peace-keeping.'
1 CONT
1 CONT See also works of Robert Torigny and Elizabeth Van Houts.Source: Church of JC of the LDS "Ancestral File" CD-Rom database, ver 4.17. Dates of last 3 children's births indicate that they may have had a younger mother than the oldes
1 CONC t two.
1 CONT
1 CONT From Gayle Wilson <gayle@inforum.net>: R. Allen Brown is of the opinion that Gunnor's father was a 'Danico', a Dane who was welcomed and permitted to settle in Normandy. Later , as more Danes appeared, this man joined their rebell
1 CONC ions and became a fierce war-leader who was giving Duke Richard trouble. Brown says that Richard married Gunnor 'in peace-keeping.'
1 CONT
1 CONT See also works of Robert Torigny and Elizabeth Van Houts.
0 @N6000000002176669886@ NOTE Harold inherited his kingdom, centered on Jelling in Jutland. Although he
1 CONT temporarily lost southern Jutland (974-983), he secured all Denmark under his
1 CONT control and extended his rule to much of Norway. He was baptized in 960, thus
1 CONT introducing Christianity to Denmark. Having consolidating the Danish realm as
1 CONT a unitary kingdom, he was fatally wounded, during a rebellion by his son and
1 CONT successor Sweyn I, in 985.
