1 CONT From his first marriage he had a son, his successor Boleslaus, and twodaughters, Sygryda and the other of an unkown name. Sygryda was thewife (as queen Sigrid the Haughty) of Eric the Victorious, king ofSweden and then (as queen G
1 CONC unhilda) of king Sweyn Forkbeard ofDenmark, and mother of king Canute of Denmark and England. The namefor such daughter, "Swietoslawa", is generally accepted amongsthistorians as best approximation on her Slavic name. The secondda
1 CONC ughter was most likely married to a Pomeranian Slavic Prince.
