0 @N6000000002322323180@ NOTE This official King of Poland, crowned personally by the Holy Roman Emperor
1 CONT Otto III in March 1000, and crowned again by the archbishop of Gniezno on
1 CONT Christmas Day, 1024, expanded his country's territory to include Pomerania,
1 CONT Lusatia, and, for a time, the Bohemian princely lands and made Poland a major
1 CONT European state. He also created a Polish church independent of German
1 CONT control. He was succeeded by his son, Mieszko II Lambert.
