0 @N6000000001579093608@ NOTE Following the defeat of her first husband, Aethelred the Unready in 1013, Emma took her two children, Alfred and Edward to Normandy for safety. Here they grew up and were influenced by French culture and ways. She returned to Engl
1 CONC and where she married Canute, leaving her children behind. In 1036, Alfred, known as the Aetheling, came to England to see his mother, possibly as a trap set up by Emma, who had no real love of the children she had with Aethelred.
1 CONT
1 CONT So affected was Edward by the way he had been treated by his mother, he removed her entitlement to her land and confiscated all her possessions.
0 @N6000000002319320881@ NOTE She represents the blood link to William I the Conqueror, as she is the
