1 CONT Mercia, Northumbria, Wessex and East Anglia, about half to Harold I, and the
1 CONT other half to half brother Hardecanute. Hardecanute would be banished by
1 CONT Harold in 1037, Leaving Harold I to be King of all England in 1037-1040.
