1 CONC of the Czechs over the other Bohemian tribes and by founding monasteries, nunneries, and capitular churches.
1 CONT Boleslav II secured the establishment of the bishopric of Prague in 973 or 974, under the metropolitan authority of the archbishops of Mainz. He treacherously but completely destroyed the Slavnikovci, the onlyprincely rivals of th
1 CONC e Premyslid dynasty in Bohemia, in 995. He was usually loyal to his suzerains, the Holy Roman emperors Otto I, II, andIII, whom he helped in their conflicts with the Polish princes, though his support of the rebellious duke of Bav
1 CONC aria, Henry the Wrangler, caused Otto II to lead punitive expeditions against him in 975 and 977-978
0 @N6000000000945084294@ NOTE Hertug av Böhmen 967 - 999. 
