0 @N6000000001353965697@ NOTE Mieszko II Lambert (b. 990--d. May 10, 1034), king of Poland from 1025 to 1034, grandson of Mieszko I. Somewhat deranged (he died mad), hewas dominated by his wife, the German Ryxa, and let the achievements of his father, Boleslaw
1 CONC  I, crumble. Much territory was lost to Bohemiaand to the Holy Roman Empire. At his death, Poland fell into anarchy.
