0 @N6000000002187746324@ NOTE Waleran IV of Limburg
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Waleran IV or Walram IV (d.1279) was the duke of Limburg from 1247 to his death. He was the son and successor of Henry IV. and Ermengarde, countess of Berg.
1 CONT
1 CONT He played a great part in the politics of the Great Interregnum in Germany. He left the Hohenstaufen fold and supported William I of Holland as king. He was sent in an embassy to Henry III of England and after William's death, sup
1 CONC ported Henry's brother Richard, Earl of Cornwall, as king. In 1272, he was party to the nobles who offerred the crown to Ottokar II of Bohemia and then Rudolph of Hapsburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1252, he intervened in the War of the Succession of Flanders and Hainault, at the side of Jean d'Avesnes. After 1258, it fell out with John I of Brabant, putting an end to sixty years of good relations with the dukes of Brabant
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT Waleran frequently intervened in the business of the archbishop of Cologne in his constant fight with the bourgeoisie of the city.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Henry IV Duke of Limburg
1 CONT 1247–1279 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Ermesinda 
0 @N6000000006127688629@ NOTE Elisabeth av Pommern, född 1290, död 1349 i Lauenburg, Schleswig-Holstein, Tyskland. Gift 1316 med hertig Erik I av Sachsen-Lauenburg, född 1275 i Lauenburg.Elisabeth och Erik fick följande barn:1. Erik II av Sachsen-Lauenburg (dö
1 CONC d 1368/1369), hertig av Sachsen-Lauenburg 2. Johan av Sachsen-Lauenburg (död 1364/1370), biskop av Kammin 3. Helene av Sachsen-Lauenburg (död efter 1354), gift med greve Johann II av Hoya-Bruchhausen (död 1377) 4. Jutta av Sachsen
1 CONC -Lauenburg (död efter 1354), gift med greve Gerhard III av Hoya (död 1383) 
